{"paragraphs":[{"text":"%python\nprint(\"Python is available in Zeppelin\")","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T18:08:02+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"python","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"Python is available in Zeppelin\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785002873840_1136643504","id":"paragraph_1785002873840_1136643504","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T18:07:53+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T18:08:02+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T18:08:04+0000","status":"FINISHED","focus":false},{"text":"%md\n## Master Task 3 – HBase Data Model\n\n### Table Name\n\n`retail_events`\n\n### Column Families\n\n#### transaction\n- transaction_id\n- event_timestamp\n- payment_type\n- loyalty_flag\n\n#### product\n- product_id\n- product_name\n- category\n\n#### store\n- store_id\n- city\n- province\n- region\n\n#### sales\n- quantity\n- unit_price\n- discount_amount\n- final_price\n- promotion_flag\n- promotion_id\n\n### Design Explanation\n\nThe table uses four column families to group related attributes.\n\n- The `transaction` family stores transaction-level information.\n- The `product` family stores product identifiers and category information.\n- The `store` family stores store and geographic information.\n- The `sales` family stores measurable sales values, discounts, and promotion information.\n\nThis organization makes the HBase schema easier to understand and supports efficient access to related attributes.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T19:06:13+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>Master Task 3 – HBase Data Model</h2>\n<h3>Table Name</h3>\n<p><code>retail_events</code></p>\n<h3>Column Families</h3>\n<h4>transaction</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>transaction_id</li>\n<li>event_timestamp</li>\n<li>payment_type</li>\n<li>loyalty_flag</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>product</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>product_id</li>\n<li>product_name</li>\n<li>category</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>store</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>store_id</li>\n<li>city</li>\n<li>province</li>\n<li>region</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>sales</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>quantity</li>\n<li>unit_price</li>\n<li>discount_amount</li>\n<li>final_price</li>\n<li>promotion_flag</li>\n<li>promotion_id</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Design Explanation</h3>\n<p>The table uses four column families to group related attributes.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>The <code>transaction</code> family stores transaction-level information.</li>\n<li>The <code>product</code> family stores product identifiers and category information.</li>\n<li>The <code>store</code> family stores store and geographic information.</li>\n<li>The <code>sales</code> family stores measurable sales values, discounts, and promotion information.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This organization makes the HBase schema easier to understand and supports efficient access to related attributes.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785002882773_232199077","id":"paragraph_1785002882773_232199077","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T18:08:02+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T19:06:13+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T19:06:15+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n## Master Task 3 – Row-Key Strategy\n\n### Row-Key Format\n\n`store_id#reverse_timestamp#event_id`\n\n### Example\n\n`ST-TOR-001#9223370260000000000#EVT-00001234`\n\n### Store Prefix\n\nThe store ID appears first so that events from the same store are stored close together. This supports store-oriented prefix scans and operational investigations.\n\n### Reverse Timestamp\n\nThe reverse timestamp is calculated as:\n\n`MAX_LONG - timestamp_in_milliseconds`\n\nNewer timestamps produce smaller reverse values. Therefore, newer events appear before older events within the same store prefix.\n\n### Event ID\n\nThe event ID guarantees uniqueness. It prevents records from overwriting one another when multiple events have the same store and timestamp.\n\n### Limitation\n\nThis row-key design is optimized for store-based access, but it does not support efficient direct lookup by transaction ID or product ID.\n\n### Hotspotting Consideration\n\nA store with a very high event volume may concentrate writes within a limited row-key range. In a large production system, salting or hashing could distribute writes more evenly, although this would make store-prefix scans more complex.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T19:07:23+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>Master Task 3 – Row-Key Strategy</h2>\n<h3>Row-Key Format</h3>\n<p><code>store_id#reverse_timestamp#event_id</code></p>\n<h3>Example</h3>\n<p><code>ST-TOR-001#9223370260000000000#EVT-00001234</code></p>\n<h3>Store Prefix</h3>\n<p>The store ID appears first so that events from the same store are stored close together. This supports store-oriented prefix scans and operational investigations.</p>\n<h3>Reverse Timestamp</h3>\n<p>The reverse timestamp is calculated as:</p>\n<p><code>MAX_LONG - timestamp_in_milliseconds</code></p>\n<p>Newer timestamps produce smaller reverse values. Therefore, newer events appear before older events within the same store prefix.</p>\n<h3>Event ID</h3>\n<p>The event ID guarantees uniqueness. It prevents records from overwriting one another when multiple events have the same store and timestamp.</p>\n<h3>Limitation</h3>\n<p>This row-key design is optimized for store-based access, but it does not support efficient direct lookup by transaction ID or product ID.</p>\n<h3>Hotspotting Consideration</h3>\n<p>A store with a very high event volume may concentrate writes within a limited row-key range. In a large production system, salting or hashing could distribute writes more evenly, although this would make store-prefix scans more complex.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785006373908_1026567071","id":"paragraph_1785006373908_1026567071","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T19:06:13+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T19:07:23+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T19:07:23+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n# Master Task 8 — Core Hive Business Analytics\n\n## Objective\n\nThis section uses Apache Hive to analyze retail event data stored in HBase.\n\nThe Hive external table `retail_events_hive` is directly connected to the HBase table `retail_events` through `HBaseStorageHandler`. Therefore, the following queries analyze the same 38,143 retail event records previously loaded into HBase.\n\n## Business Questions\n\nThe analysis focuses on the following questions:\n\n1. Which stores generate the highest revenue?\n2. Which product categories perform best?\n3. Which payment methods are most frequently used?\n4. How do loyalty customers compare with non-loyalty customers?\n5. What is the impact of promotions on sales?\n6. Which products have the highest sales volume and revenue?\n\n## Dataset Validation\n\nBefore performing business analysis, the dataset is validated by confirming the total number of retail events and distinct transactions.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T21:25:39+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h1>Master Task 8 — Core Hive Business Analytics</h1>\n<h2>Objective</h2>\n<p>This section uses Apache Hive to analyze retail event data stored in HBase.</p>\n<p>The Hive external table <code>retail_events_hive</code> is directly connected to the HBase table <code>retail_events</code> through <code>HBaseStorageHandler</code>. Therefore, the following queries analyze the same 38,143 retail event records previously loaded into HBase.</p>\n<h2>Business Questions</h2>\n<p>The analysis focuses on the following questions:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Which stores generate the highest revenue?</li>\n<li>Which product categories perform best?</li>\n<li>Which payment methods are most frequently used?</li>\n<li>How do loyalty customers compare with non-loyalty customers?</li>\n<li>What is the impact of promotions on sales?</li>\n<li>Which products have the highest sales volume and revenue?</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Dataset Validation</h2>\n<p>Before performing business analysis, the dataset is validated by confirming the total number of retail events and distinct transactions.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785006443238_1152138513","id":"paragraph_1785006443238_1152138513","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T19:07:23+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T21:25:39+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T21:25:39+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nSELECT\n    COUNT(*) AS total_events,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT transaction_id) AS total_transactions,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT store_id) AS total_stores,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT product_id) AS total_products\nFROM retail_events_hive;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T21:25:58+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"INFO  : Compiling command(queryId=root_20260725212559_2a62825a-c623-40b2-ac55-ca3e4320ff5a): \n\nSELECT\n    COUNT(*) AS total_events,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT transaction_id) AS total_transactions,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT store_id) AS total_stores,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT product_id) AS total_products\nFROM retail_events_hive\nINFO  : No Stats for default@retail_events_hive, Columns: transaction_id, store_id, product_id\nINFO  : Semantic Analysis Completed (retrial = false)\nINFO  : Created Hive schema: Schema(fieldSchemas:[FieldSchema(name:total_events, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_transactions, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_stores, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_products, type:bigint, comment:null)], properties:null)\nINFO  : Completed compiling command(queryId=root_20260725212559_2a62825a-c623-40b2-ac55-ca3e4320ff5a); Time taken: 0.104 seconds\nINFO  : Concurrency mode is disabled, not creating a lock manager\nINFO  : Executing command(queryId=root_20260725212559_2a62825a-c623-40b2-ac55-ca3e4320ff5a): \n\nSELECT\n    COUNT(*) AS total_events,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT transaction_id) AS total_transactions,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT store_id) AS total_stores,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT product_id) AS total_products\nFROM retail_events_hive\nWARN  : Hive-on-MR is deprecated in Hive 2 and may not be available in the future versions. Consider using a different execution engine (i.e. tez) or using Hive 1.X releases.\nINFO  : Query ID = root_20260725212559_2a62825a-c623-40b2-ac55-ca3e4320ff5a\nINFO  : Total jobs = 1\nINFO  : Launching Job 1 out of 1\nINFO  : Starting task [Stage-1:MAPRED] in serial mode\nINFO  : Number of reduce tasks determined at compile time: 1\nINFO  : In order to change the average load for a reducer (in bytes):\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.bytes.per.reducer=<number>\nINFO  : In order to limit the maximum number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.max=<number>\nINFO  : In order to set a constant number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set mapreduce.job.reduces=<number>\n"},{"type":"TABLE","data":"total_events\ttotal_transactions\ttotal_stores\ttotal_products\n38143\t12725\t12\t45\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785014739266_217522444","id":"paragraph_1785014739266_217522444","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T21:25:39+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T21:25:58+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T21:26:26+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n### Dataset Validation Result\n\nThe Hive query confirms that the external table contains **38,143 retail event records** and **12,725 distinct transactions**.\n\nThis result matches the original dataset and the HBase record count. It confirms that Hive is successfully reading the complete retail dataset directly from HBase.\n\nThe validated dataset can now be used for the following business analytics.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T21:26:49+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Dataset Validation Result</h3>\n<p>The Hive query confirms that the external table contains <strong>38,143 retail event records</strong> and <strong>12,725 distinct transactions</strong>.</p>\n<p>This result matches the original dataset and the HBase record count. It confirms that Hive is successfully reading the complete retail dataset directly from HBase.</p>\n<p>The validated dataset can now be used for the following business analytics.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785014758016_1824628019","id":"paragraph_1785014758016_1824628019","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T21:25:58+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T21:26:49+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T21:26:49+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n## 1. Revenue by Store\n\n### Business Question\n\nWhich stores generate the highest total revenue?\n\n### Analysis Method\n\nThe query groups retail event records by store and calculates:\n\n- Total number of sales events\n- Total quantity sold\n- Total revenue\n- Average revenue per sales event\n\nThe stores are ranked from the highest to the lowest total revenue.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T21:40:12+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>1. Revenue by Store</h2>\n<h3>Business Question</h3>\n<p>Which stores generate the highest total revenue?</p>\n<h3>Analysis Method</h3>\n<p>The query groups retail event records by store and calculates:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Total number of sales events</li>\n<li>Total quantity sold</li>\n<li>Total revenue</li>\n<li>Average revenue per sales event</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The stores are ranked from the highest to the lowest total revenue.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785014809092_1465011145","id":"paragraph_1785014809092_1465011145","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T21:26:49+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T21:40:12+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T21:40:13+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nSELECT\n    store_id,\n    store_city,\n    store_region,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY\n    store_id,\n    store_city,\n    store_region\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T21:48:26+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{"1":{"graph":{"mode":"multiBarChart","height":298.5078125,"optionOpen":true,"setting":{"multiBarChart":{"rotate":{"degree":"-45"},"xLabelStatus":"default","stacked":false}},"keys":[{"name":"store_id","index":0,"aggr":"sum"}],"groups":[],"values":[{"name":"total_revenue","index":5,"aggr":"sum"}]}}},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"INFO  : Compiling command(queryId=root_20260725214029_4e0ded98-4122-4c79-b756-f442e5790d63): \n\nSELECT\n    store_id,\n    store_city,\n    store_region,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY\n    store_id,\n    store_city,\n    store_region\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC\nINFO  : No Stats for default@retail_events_hive, Columns: store_id, store_city, quantity, final_price, store_region\nINFO  : Semantic Analysis Completed (retrial = false)\nINFO  : Created Hive schema: Schema(fieldSchemas:[FieldSchema(name:store_id, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:store_city, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:store_region, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:sales_events, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_quantity, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_revenue, type:double, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:average_event_value, type:double, comment:null)], properties:null)\nINFO  : Completed compiling command(queryId=root_20260725214029_4e0ded98-4122-4c79-b756-f442e5790d63); Time taken: 0.233 seconds\nINFO  : Concurrency mode is disabled, not creating a lock manager\nINFO  : Executing command(queryId=root_20260725214029_4e0ded98-4122-4c79-b756-f442e5790d63): \n\nSELECT\n    store_id,\n    store_city,\n    store_region,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY\n    store_id,\n    store_city,\n    store_region\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC\nWARN  : Hive-on-MR is deprecated in Hive 2 and may not be available in the future versions. Consider using a different execution engine (i.e. tez) or using Hive 1.X releases.\nINFO  : Query ID = root_20260725214029_4e0ded98-4122-4c79-b756-f442e5790d63\nINFO  : Total jobs = 2\nINFO  : Launching Job 1 out of 2\nINFO  : Starting task [Stage-1:MAPRED] in serial mode\nINFO  : Number of reduce tasks not specified. Estimated from input data size: 1\nINFO  : In order to change the average load for a reducer (in bytes):\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.bytes.per.reducer=<number>\nINFO  : In order to limit the maximum number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.max=<number>\nINFO  : In order to set a constant number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set mapreduce.job.reduces=<number>\n"},{"type":"TABLE","data":"store_id\tstore_city\tstore_region\tsales_events\ttotal_quantity\ttotal_revenue\taverage_event_value\nST-CAL-001\tCalgary\tWestern\t3453\t6046\t55573.77\t16.09\nST-TOR-001\tToronto\tCentral\t3855\t5894\t54080.88\t14.03\nST-TOR-002\tToronto\tCentral\t3495\t5318\t49425.3\t14.14\nST-OTT-001\tOttawa\tEastern\t3515\t5334\t48425.04\t13.78\nST-MIS-001\tMississauga\tCentral\t3421\t5236\t47075.34\t13.76\nST-EDM-001\tEdmonton\tWestern\t3308\t5056\t46308.45\t14.0\nST-BRA-001\tBrampton\tCentral\t2932\t4451\t40625.77\t13.86\nST-SCA-001\tScarborough\tCentral\t2879\t4425\t40277.22\t13.99\nST-OTT-002\tOttawa\tEastern\t2864\t4386\t40078.66\t13.99\nST-LON-001\tLondon\tCentral\t2812\t4289\t40069.41\t14.25\nST-HAM-001\tHamilton\tCentral\t2824\t4352\t39916.22\t14.13\nST-KIT-001\tKitchener\tCentral\t2785\t4149\t37874.89\t13.6\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785015612994_1500095350","id":"paragraph_1785015612994_1500095350","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T21:40:12+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T21:40:29+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T21:41:08+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n### Interpretation\n\nThe store with the highest total revenue is **ST-CAL-001**, located in **Calgary**.\n\nThis store generated approximately **$55,573.77** in total revenue and sold **6046** units.\n\nThe result suggests that this location has stronger customer traffic, higher product demand, or a larger average purchase value than the other stores.\n\nManagement could further examine this store's product mix, customer profile, and promotional strategy to identify practices that could be applied to lower-performing stores.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T21:54:32+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Interpretation</h3>\n<p>The store with the highest total revenue is <strong>ST-CAL-001</strong>, located in <strong>Calgary</strong>.</p>\n<p>This store generated approximately <strong>$55,573.77</strong> in total revenue and sold <strong>6046</strong> units.</p>\n<p>The result suggests that this location has stronger customer traffic, higher product demand, or a larger average purchase value than the other stores.</p>\n<p>Management could further examine this store&rsquo;s product mix, customer profile, and promotional strategy to identify practices that could be applied to lower-performing stores.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785015629035_106665741","id":"paragraph_1785015629035_106665741","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T21:40:29+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T21:54:32+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T21:54:32+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n## 2. Sales by Product Category\n\n### Business Question\n\nWhich product categories generate the highest sales volume and revenue?\n\n### Analysis Method\n\nThe query groups retail event records by product category and calculates:\n\n- Number of sales events\n- Total quantity sold\n- Total revenue\n- Average revenue per sales event\n\nThe categories are ranked from the highest to the lowest total revenue.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T21:51:41+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>2. Sales by Product Category</h2>\n<h3>Business Question</h3>\n<p>Which product categories generate the highest sales volume and revenue?</p>\n<h3>Analysis Method</h3>\n<p>The query groups retail event records by product category and calculates:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Number of sales events</li>\n<li>Total quantity sold</li>\n<li>Total revenue</li>\n<li>Average revenue per sales event</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The categories are ranked from the highest to the lowest total revenue.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785016030983_1427708759","id":"paragraph_1785016030983_1427708759","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T21:47:10+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T21:51:41+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T21:51:41+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nSELECT\n    category,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY category\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T21:55:01+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{"1":{"graph":{"mode":"multiBarChart","height":300,"optionOpen":true,"setting":{"multiBarChart":{"rotate":{"degree":"-45"},"xLabelStatus":"default","stacked":false}},"keys":[{"name":"category","index":0,"aggr":"sum"}],"groups":[],"values":[{"name":"total_revenue","index":3,"aggr":"sum"}]}}},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"INFO  : Compiling command(queryId=root_20260725215201_dad243c3-3df8-4262-bc99-d9bb506a5762): \n\nSELECT\n    category,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY category\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC\nINFO  : No Stats for default@retail_events_hive, Columns: quantity, final_price, category\nINFO  : Semantic Analysis Completed (retrial = false)\nINFO  : Created Hive schema: Schema(fieldSchemas:[FieldSchema(name:category, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:sales_events, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_quantity, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_revenue, type:double, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:average_event_value, type:double, comment:null)], properties:null)\nINFO  : Completed compiling command(queryId=root_20260725215201_dad243c3-3df8-4262-bc99-d9bb506a5762); Time taken: 0.148 seconds\nINFO  : Concurrency mode is disabled, not creating a lock manager\nINFO  : Executing command(queryId=root_20260725215201_dad243c3-3df8-4262-bc99-d9bb506a5762): \n\nSELECT\n    category,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY category\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC\nWARN  : Hive-on-MR is deprecated in Hive 2 and may not be available in the future versions. Consider using a different execution engine (i.e. tez) or using Hive 1.X releases.\nINFO  : Query ID = root_20260725215201_dad243c3-3df8-4262-bc99-d9bb506a5762\nINFO  : Total jobs = 2\nINFO  : Launching Job 1 out of 2\nINFO  : Starting task [Stage-1:MAPRED] in serial mode\nINFO  : Number of reduce tasks not specified. Estimated from input data size: 1\nINFO  : In order to change the average load for a reducer (in bytes):\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.bytes.per.reducer=<number>\nINFO  : In order to limit the maximum number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.max=<number>\nINFO  : In order to set a constant number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set mapreduce.job.reduces=<number>\n"},{"type":"TABLE","data":"category\tsales_events\ttotal_quantity\ttotal_revenue\taverage_event_value\nGrocery\t11388\t17653\t171287.76\t15.04\nProduce\t5678\t8704\t73399.93\t12.93\nDairy\t5748\t8902\t70165.09\t12.21\nHousehold\t3110\t4771\t61643.25\t19.82\nFrozen\t3065\t4721\t60305.89\t19.68\nBakery\t3091\t4770\t41660.92\t13.48\nMeat\t3053\t4710\t32212.84\t10.55\nPersonal Care\t3010\t4705\t29055.27\t9.65\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785016301579_236970215","id":"paragraph_1785016301579_236970215","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T21:51:41+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T21:52:01+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T21:52:42+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n### Interpretation\n\nThe category with the highest total revenue is **Grocery**.\n\nIt generated approximately **$171,287.76** in revenue from **17653** units sold.\n\nThis result indicates that the category is a major contributor to overall retail performance. Management should ensure sufficient inventory levels and examine whether targeted promotions could further strengthen its sales.\n\nLower-performing categories may require adjustments in pricing, product selection, inventory allocation, or promotional strategy.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T21:54:20+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Interpretation</h3>\n<p>The category with the highest total revenue is <strong>Grocery</strong>.</p>\n<p>It generated approximately <strong>$171,287.76</strong> in revenue from <strong>17653</strong> units sold.</p>\n<p>This result indicates that the category is a major contributor to overall retail performance. Management should ensure sufficient inventory levels and examine whether targeted promotions could further strengthen its sales.</p>\n<p>Lower-performing categories may require adjustments in pricing, product selection, inventory allocation, or promotional strategy.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785016321841_1666165405","id":"paragraph_1785016321841_1666165405","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T21:52:01+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T21:54:20+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T21:54:20+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n## 3. Payment Type Analysis\n\n### Business Question\n\nWhich payment methods are most frequently used, and which payment methods generate the highest total revenue?\n\n### Analysis Method\n\nThe query groups retail event records by payment type and calculates:\n\n- Number of sales events\n- Number of distinct transactions\n- Total quantity sold\n- Total revenue\n- Average revenue per sales event\n\nThe payment methods are ranked from the highest to the lowest total revenue.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T21:58:28+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>3. Payment Type Analysis</h2>\n<h3>Business Question</h3>\n<p>Which payment methods are most frequently used, and which payment methods generate the highest total revenue?</p>\n<h3>Analysis Method</h3>\n<p>The query groups retail event records by payment type and calculates:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Number of sales events</li>\n<li>Number of distinct transactions</li>\n<li>Total quantity sold</li>\n<li>Total revenue</li>\n<li>Average revenue per sales event</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The payment methods are ranked from the highest to the lowest total revenue.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785016460322_912092588","id":"paragraph_1785016460322_912092588","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T21:54:20+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T21:58:28+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T21:58:28+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nSELECT\n    payment_type,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT transaction_id) AS total_transactions,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY payment_type\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:04:14+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{"1":{"graph":{"mode":"multiBarChart","height":300,"optionOpen":true,"setting":{"multiBarChart":{"rotate":{"degree":"-45"},"xLabelStatus":"default","stacked":false}},"keys":[{"name":"payment_type","index":0,"aggr":"sum"}],"groups":[],"values":[{"name":"total_transactions","index":2,"aggr":"sum"},{"name":"total_revenue","index":4,"aggr":"sum"}]}}},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"INFO  : Compiling command(queryId=root_20260725215840_d65f085c-e5b0-466c-9bef-419c88d348ba): \n\nSELECT\n    payment_type,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT transaction_id) AS total_transactions,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY payment_type\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC\nINFO  : No Stats for default@retail_events_hive, Columns: transaction_id, payment_type, quantity, final_price\nINFO  : Semantic Analysis Completed (retrial = false)\nINFO  : Created Hive schema: Schema(fieldSchemas:[FieldSchema(name:payment_type, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:sales_events, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_transactions, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_quantity, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_revenue, type:double, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:average_event_value, type:double, comment:null)], properties:null)\nINFO  : Completed compiling command(queryId=root_20260725215840_d65f085c-e5b0-466c-9bef-419c88d348ba); Time taken: 0.155 seconds\nINFO  : Concurrency mode is disabled, not creating a lock manager\nINFO  : Executing command(queryId=root_20260725215840_d65f085c-e5b0-466c-9bef-419c88d348ba): \n\nSELECT\n    payment_type,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT transaction_id) AS total_transactions,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY payment_type\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC\nWARN  : Hive-on-MR is deprecated in Hive 2 and may not be available in the future versions. Consider using a different execution engine (i.e. tez) or using Hive 1.X releases.\nINFO  : Query ID = root_20260725215840_d65f085c-e5b0-466c-9bef-419c88d348ba\nINFO  : Total jobs = 2\nINFO  : Launching Job 1 out of 2\nINFO  : Starting task [Stage-1:MAPRED] in serial mode\nINFO  : Number of reduce tasks not specified. Estimated from input data size: 1\nINFO  : In order to change the average load for a reducer (in bytes):\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.bytes.per.reducer=<number>\nINFO  : In order to limit the maximum number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.max=<number>\nINFO  : In order to set a constant number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set mapreduce.job.reduces=<number>\n"},{"type":"TABLE","data":"payment_type\tsales_events\ttotal_transactions\ttotal_quantity\ttotal_revenue\taverage_event_value\nCredit\t16384\t5504\t25259\t232109.16\t14.17\nDebit\t14119\t4681\t21821\t199286.08\t14.11\nCash\t4628\t1521\t7196\t66264.63\t14.32\nMobile\t3012\t1019\t4660\t42071.08\t13.97\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785016708628_762372209","id":"paragraph_1785016708628_762372209","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T21:58:28+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T21:58:40+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T21:59:19+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n### Interpretation\n\n**Credit** generated the highest total revenue, reaching approximately **$232,109.16** across **5504** distinct transactions.\n\nThis payment method also accounted for **16384** individual sales events.\n\nThe result indicates that **Credit** is an important payment channel for the retailer. The company should ensure that this payment method remains reliable, convenient, and widely available across all store locations.\n\nComparing total transactions with average event value also helps determine whether a payment method performs strongly because it is used frequently or because customers spend more per sales event.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:01:19+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Interpretation</h3>\n<p><strong>Credit</strong> generated the highest total revenue, reaching approximately <strong>$232,109.16</strong> across <strong>5504</strong> distinct transactions.</p>\n<p>This payment method also accounted for <strong>16384</strong> individual sales events.</p>\n<p>The result indicates that <strong>Credit</strong> is an important payment channel for the retailer. The company should ensure that this payment method remains reliable, convenient, and widely available across all store locations.</p>\n<p>Comparing total transactions with average event value also helps determine whether a payment method performs strongly because it is used frequently or because customers spend more per sales event.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785016720489_1503238700","id":"paragraph_1785016720489_1503238700","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T21:58:40+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:01:19+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:01:19+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n## 4. Loyalty Customer Comparison\n\n### Business Question\n\nHow do loyalty customers compare with non-loyalty customers in terms of transaction activity, quantity purchased, and total revenue?\n\n### Analysis Method\n\nThe query groups retail event records by loyalty status and calculates:\n\n- Number of sales events\n- Number of distinct transactions\n- Total quantity purchased\n- Total revenue\n- Average revenue per sales event\n\nThis comparison helps determine whether loyalty customers contribute more strongly to overall retail performance.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:06:01+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>4. Loyalty Customer Comparison</h2>\n<h3>Business Question</h3>\n<p>How do loyalty customers compare with non-loyalty customers in terms of transaction activity, quantity purchased, and total revenue?</p>\n<h3>Analysis Method</h3>\n<p>The query groups retail event records by loyalty status and calculates:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Number of sales events</li>\n<li>Number of distinct transactions</li>\n<li>Total quantity purchased</li>\n<li>Total revenue</li>\n<li>Average revenue per sales event</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This comparison helps determine whether loyalty customers contribute more strongly to overall retail performance.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785016879191_1030123265","id":"paragraph_1785016879191_1030123265","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:01:19+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:06:01+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:06:01+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nSELECT\n    loyalty_flag,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT transaction_id) AS total_transactions,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY loyalty_flag\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:27:48+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{"1":{"graph":{"mode":"multiBarChart","height":300,"optionOpen":true,"setting":{"multiBarChart":{"rotate":{"degree":"-45"},"xLabelStatus":"default","stacked":false}},"keys":[{"name":"loyalty_flag","index":0,"aggr":"sum"}],"groups":[],"values":[{"name":"total_transactions","index":2,"aggr":"sum"},{"name":"total_revenue","index":4,"aggr":"sum"}]}}},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"INFO  : Compiling command(queryId=root_20260725220619_9ed26848-55fd-48e5-8c03-1cf0b5017203): \n\nSELECT\n    loyalty_flag,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT transaction_id) AS total_transactions,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY loyalty_flag\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC\nINFO  : No Stats for default@retail_events_hive, Columns: transaction_id, loyalty_flag, quantity, final_price\nINFO  : Semantic Analysis Completed (retrial = false)\nINFO  : Created Hive schema: Schema(fieldSchemas:[FieldSchema(name:loyalty_flag, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:sales_events, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_transactions, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_quantity, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_revenue, type:double, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:average_event_value, type:double, comment:null)], properties:null)\nINFO  : Completed compiling command(queryId=root_20260725220619_9ed26848-55fd-48e5-8c03-1cf0b5017203); Time taken: 0.204 seconds\nINFO  : Concurrency mode is disabled, not creating a lock manager\nINFO  : Executing command(queryId=root_20260725220619_9ed26848-55fd-48e5-8c03-1cf0b5017203): \n\nSELECT\n    loyalty_flag,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT transaction_id) AS total_transactions,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY loyalty_flag\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC\nWARN  : Hive-on-MR is deprecated in Hive 2 and may not be available in the future versions. Consider using a different execution engine (i.e. tez) or using Hive 1.X releases.\nINFO  : Query ID = root_20260725220619_9ed26848-55fd-48e5-8c03-1cf0b5017203\nINFO  : Total jobs = 2\nINFO  : Launching Job 1 out of 2\nINFO  : Starting task [Stage-1:MAPRED] in serial mode\nINFO  : Number of reduce tasks not specified. Estimated from input data size: 1\nINFO  : In order to change the average load for a reducer (in bytes):\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.bytes.per.reducer=<number>\nINFO  : In order to limit the maximum number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.max=<number>\nINFO  : In order to set a constant number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set mapreduce.job.reduces=<number>\n"},{"type":"TABLE","data":"loyalty_flag\tsales_events\ttotal_transactions\ttotal_quantity\ttotal_revenue\taverage_event_value\nY\t25931\t8701\t39953\t364559.47\t14.06\nN\t12212\t4024\t18983\t175171.48\t14.34\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785017161257_347066082","id":"paragraph_1785017161257_347066082","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:06:01+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:06:19+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:06:58+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n### Interpretation\n\nCustomers with loyalty status **Loyalty customer** generated the higher total revenue, reaching approximately **$364,559.47**.\n\nThey completed **8701** distinct transactions and purchased a total of **39953** units.\n\nThis result suggests that **LOYALTY customers** make a stronger contribution to overall retail performance.\n\nIf loyalty customers generate higher revenue, the company should continue strengthening its loyalty program through personalized promotions, rewards, and targeted product recommendations.\n\nIf non-loyalty customers generate higher revenue, the company could focus on converting more of these customers into loyalty members to improve customer retention and support future repeat purchases.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:27:35+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Interpretation</h3>\n<p>Customers with loyalty status <strong>Loyalty customer</strong> generated the higher total revenue, reaching approximately <strong>$364,559.47</strong>.</p>\n<p>They completed <strong>8701</strong> distinct transactions and purchased a total of <strong>39953</strong> units.</p>\n<p>This result suggests that <strong>LOYALTY customers</strong> make a stronger contribution to overall retail performance.</p>\n<p>If loyalty customers generate higher revenue, the company should continue strengthening its loyalty program through personalized promotions, rewards, and targeted product recommendations.</p>\n<p>If non-loyalty customers generate higher revenue, the company could focus on converting more of these customers into loyalty members to improve customer retention and support future repeat purchases.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785017179042_1969961492","id":"paragraph_1785017179042_1969961492","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:06:19+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:27:35+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:27:35+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n## 5. Promotion Impact Analysis\n\n### Business Question\n\nHow do promoted sales events compare with non-promoted sales events in terms of transaction activity, quantity sold, and total revenue?\n\n### Analysis Method\n\nThe query groups retail event records by promotion status and calculates:\n\n- Number of sales events\n- Number of distinct transactions\n- Total quantity sold\n- Total discount amount\n- Total revenue\n- Average revenue per sales event\n\nThis comparison helps evaluate whether promotional activities are associated with higher sales volume and stronger revenue performance.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:16:26+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>5. Promotion Impact Analysis</h2>\n<h3>Business Question</h3>\n<p>How do promoted sales events compare with non-promoted sales events in terms of transaction activity, quantity sold, and total revenue?</p>\n<h3>Analysis Method</h3>\n<p>The query groups retail event records by promotion status and calculates:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Number of sales events</li>\n<li>Number of distinct transactions</li>\n<li>Total quantity sold</li>\n<li>Total discount amount</li>\n<li>Total revenue</li>\n<li>Average revenue per sales event</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This comparison helps evaluate whether promotional activities are associated with higher sales volume and stronger revenue performance.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785017695536_588115627","id":"paragraph_1785017695536_588115627","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:14:55+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:16:26+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:16:26+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nSELECT\n    promotion_flag,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT transaction_id) AS total_transactions,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(discount_amount AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_discount,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY promotion_flag\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:29:40+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{"1":{"graph":{"mode":"multiBarChart","height":300,"optionOpen":true,"setting":{"multiBarChart":{"rotate":{"degree":"-45"},"xLabelStatus":"default","stacked":false}},"keys":[{"name":"promotion_flag","index":0,"aggr":"sum"}],"groups":[],"values":[{"name":"total_revenue","index":5,"aggr":"sum"},{"name":"total_quantity","index":3,"aggr":"sum"}]}}},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"INFO  : Compiling command(queryId=root_20260725221636_9283be68-40cc-4e9b-aa1a-3505babc521c): \n\nSELECT\n    promotion_flag,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT transaction_id) AS total_transactions,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(discount_amount AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_discount,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY promotion_flag\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC\nINFO  : No Stats for default@retail_events_hive, Columns: transaction_id, quantity, final_price, discount_amount, promotion_flag\nINFO  : Semantic Analysis Completed (retrial = false)\nINFO  : Created Hive schema: Schema(fieldSchemas:[FieldSchema(name:promotion_flag, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:sales_events, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_transactions, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_quantity, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_discount, type:double, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_revenue, type:double, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:average_event_value, type:double, comment:null)], properties:null)\nINFO  : Completed compiling command(queryId=root_20260725221636_9283be68-40cc-4e9b-aa1a-3505babc521c); Time taken: 0.147 seconds\nINFO  : Concurrency mode is disabled, not creating a lock manager\nINFO  : Executing command(queryId=root_20260725221636_9283be68-40cc-4e9b-aa1a-3505babc521c): \n\nSELECT\n    promotion_flag,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT transaction_id) AS total_transactions,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(discount_amount AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_discount,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY promotion_flag\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC\nWARN  : Hive-on-MR is deprecated in Hive 2 and may not be available in the future versions. Consider using a different execution engine (i.e. tez) or using Hive 1.X releases.\nINFO  : Query ID = root_20260725221636_9283be68-40cc-4e9b-aa1a-3505babc521c\nINFO  : Total jobs = 2\nINFO  : Launching Job 1 out of 2\nINFO  : Starting task [Stage-1:MAPRED] in serial mode\nINFO  : Number of reduce tasks not specified. Estimated from input data size: 1\nINFO  : In order to change the average load for a reducer (in bytes):\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.bytes.per.reducer=<number>\nINFO  : In order to limit the maximum number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.max=<number>\nINFO  : In order to set a constant number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set mapreduce.job.reduces=<number>\n"},{"type":"TABLE","data":"promotion_flag\tsales_events\ttotal_transactions\ttotal_quantity\ttotal_discount\ttotal_revenue\taverage_event_value\nN\t37037\t12686\t57261\t0.0\t522320.56\t14.1\nY\t1106\t1081\t1675\t3552.79\t17410.39\t15.74\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785017786627_602721596","id":"paragraph_1785017786627_602721596","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:16:26+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:16:36+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:17:14+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n### Interpretation\n\nSales events with promotion status **Non-promotional sales event** generated the higher total revenue, reaching approximately **$522,320.56**.\n\nThese sales events included **12686** distinct transactions and **57261** units sold. The total discount amount was approximately **$0.0**.\n\nThis result shows whether promotional sales or regular sales contributed more strongly to the retailer's overall revenue.\n\nIf promoted sales generated higher quantity but lower average event value, the promotions may have encouraged customers to purchase more items at reduced prices.\n\nIf non-promoted sales generated higher revenue, the result may indicate that regular-priced products remain the primary source of revenue. Management should therefore evaluate both sales volume and discount cost before expanding future promotional campaigns.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:26:11+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Interpretation</h3>\n<p>Sales events with promotion status <strong>Non-promotional sales event</strong> generated the higher total revenue, reaching approximately <strong>$522,320.56</strong>.</p>\n<p>These sales events included <strong>12686</strong> distinct transactions and <strong>57261</strong> units sold. The total discount amount was approximately <strong>$0.0</strong>.</p>\n<p>This result shows whether promotional sales or regular sales contributed more strongly to the retailer&rsquo;s overall revenue.</p>\n<p>If promoted sales generated higher quantity but lower average event value, the promotions may have encouraged customers to purchase more items at reduced prices.</p>\n<p>If non-promoted sales generated higher revenue, the result may indicate that regular-priced products remain the primary source of revenue. Management should therefore evaluate both sales volume and discount cost before expanding future promotional campaigns.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785017796319_1506817930","id":"paragraph_1785017796319_1506817930","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:16:36+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:26:11+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:26:11+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n## 6. Top-Selling Products Analysis\n\n### Business Question\n\nWhich products generate the highest sales volume and total revenue?\n\n### Analysis Method\n\nThe query groups retail event records by product and calculates:\n\n- Number of sales events\n- Total quantity sold\n- Total revenue\n- Average revenue per sales event\n\nThe products are ranked by total revenue, and only the top 10 products are displayed to keep the results and visualization clear.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:31:01+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>6. Top-Selling Products Analysis</h2>\n<h3>Business Question</h3>\n<p>Which products generate the highest sales volume and total revenue?</p>\n<h3>Analysis Method</h3>\n<p>The query groups retail event records by product and calculates:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Number of sales events</li>\n<li>Total quantity sold</li>\n<li>Total revenue</li>\n<li>Average revenue per sales event</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The products are ranked by total revenue, and only the top 10 products are displayed to keep the results and visualization clear.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785018371499_209866231","id":"paragraph_1785018371499_209866231","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:26:11+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:31:01+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:31:01+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nSELECT\n    product_id,\n    product_name,\n    category,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY\n    product_id,\n    product_name,\n    category\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC\nLIMIT 10;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:36:19+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{"1":{"graph":{"mode":"multiBarChart","height":300,"optionOpen":true,"setting":{"multiBarChart":{"rotate":{"degree":"-45"},"xLabelStatus":"default","stacked":false}},"keys":[{"name":"product_id","index":0,"aggr":"sum"}],"groups":[],"values":[{"name":"total_revenue","index":5,"aggr":"sum"}]}}},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"INFO  : Compiling command(queryId=root_20260725223110_23e3a12f-615c-46c8-8bcd-fadce84e4bbc): \n\nSELECT\n    product_id,\n    product_name,\n    category,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY\n    product_id,\n    product_name,\n    category\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC\nLIMIT 10\nINFO  : No Stats for default@retail_events_hive, Columns: quantity, final_price, product_id, category, product_name\nINFO  : Semantic Analysis Completed (retrial = false)\nINFO  : Created Hive schema: Schema(fieldSchemas:[FieldSchema(name:product_id, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:product_name, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:category, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:sales_events, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_quantity, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_revenue, type:double, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:average_event_value, type:double, comment:null)], properties:null)\nINFO  : Completed compiling command(queryId=root_20260725223110_23e3a12f-615c-46c8-8bcd-fadce84e4bbc); Time taken: 0.136 seconds\nINFO  : Concurrency mode is disabled, not creating a lock manager\nINFO  : Executing command(queryId=root_20260725223110_23e3a12f-615c-46c8-8bcd-fadce84e4bbc): \n\nSELECT\n    product_id,\n    product_name,\n    category,\n    COUNT(*) AS sales_events,\n    SUM(CAST(quantity AS INT)) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(CAST(final_price AS DOUBLE)), 2) AS average_event_value\nFROM retail_events_hive\nGROUP BY\n    product_id,\n    product_name,\n    category\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC\nLIMIT 10\nWARN  : Hive-on-MR is deprecated in Hive 2 and may not be available in the future versions. Consider using a different execution engine (i.e. tez) or using Hive 1.X releases.\nINFO  : Query ID = root_20260725223110_23e3a12f-615c-46c8-8bcd-fadce84e4bbc\nINFO  : Total jobs = 2\nINFO  : Launching Job 1 out of 2\nINFO  : Starting task [Stage-1:MAPRED] in serial mode\nINFO  : Number of reduce tasks not specified. Estimated from input data size: 1\nINFO  : In order to change the average load for a reducer (in bytes):\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.bytes.per.reducer=<number>\nINFO  : In order to limit the maximum number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.max=<number>\nINFO  : In order to set a constant number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set mapreduce.job.reduces=<number>\n"},{"type":"TABLE","data":"product_id\tproduct_name\tcategory\tsales_events\ttotal_quantity\ttotal_revenue\taverage_event_value\nP025\tCoffee 900g\tGrocery\t1128\t1727\t28880.83\t25.6\nP029\tOrange Juice 2.5L\tGrocery\t1151\t1781\t27634.31\t24.01\nP007\tApples 3lb\tProduce\t1102\t1648\t26741.98\t24.27\nP021\tPasta 900g\tGrocery\t1141\t1738\t25774.95\t22.59\nP005\tButter 454g\tDairy\t1120\t1745\t23940.67\t21.38\nP022\tTomato Sauce\tGrocery\t1155\t1816\t23808.58\t20.61\nP006\tBananas\tProduce\t1153\t1760\t21920.02\t19.01\nP001\t2% Milk 4L\tDairy\t1171\t1819\t21738.85\t18.56\nP030\tSparkling Water 12pk\tGrocery\t1107\t1744\t20177.36\t18.23\nP034\tFrozen Vegetables 750g\tFrozen\t616\t925\t16244.1\t26.37\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785018661693_1568229507","id":"paragraph_1785018661693_1568229507","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:31:01+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:31:10+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:31:47+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n### Interpretation\n\nThe highest-revenue product is **Coffee 900g** in the **Grocery** category.\n\nIt generated approximately **$28,880.83** in total revenue from **1727** units sold across **1128** sales events.\n\nThis result shows that the product is an important contributor to overall retail performance. Management should maintain sufficient inventory and monitor its availability across store locations.\n\nThe remaining top-ranked products should also receive attention in inventory planning, pricing decisions, and promotional campaigns because product shortages could directly affect revenue.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:35:59+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Interpretation</h3>\n<p>The highest-revenue product is <strong>Coffee 900g</strong> in the <strong>Grocery</strong> category.</p>\n<p>It generated approximately <strong>$28,880.83</strong> in total revenue from <strong>1727</strong> units sold across <strong>1128</strong> sales events.</p>\n<p>This result shows that the product is an important contributor to overall retail performance. Management should maintain sufficient inventory and monitor its availability across store locations.</p>\n<p>The remaining top-ranked products should also receive attention in inventory planning, pricing decisions, and promotional campaigns because product shortages could directly affect revenue.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785018670683_360879432","id":"paragraph_1785018670683_360879432","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:31:10+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:35:59+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:35:59+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n# Master Task 9 — Advanced Hive Analytics and Visualizations\n\n## Objective\n\nThis section extends the core business analysis by creating a typed Hive analytical view and performing advanced retail analytics.\n\nThe analysis includes:\n\n- Transaction-level performance\n- Regional comparisons\n- Time-based activity\n- Category contribution\n- Promotion performance by category\n- Store ranking and performance deviation\n\nThe majority of the analysis is performed in HiveQL and visualized in Apache Zeppelin.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:38:12+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h1>Master Task 9 — Advanced Hive Analytics and Visualizations</h1>\n<h2>Objective</h2>\n<p>This section extends the core business analysis by creating a typed Hive analytical view and performing advanced retail analytics.</p>\n<p>The analysis includes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Transaction-level performance</li>\n<li>Regional comparisons</li>\n<li>Time-based activity</li>\n<li>Category contribution</li>\n<li>Promotion performance by category</li>\n<li>Store ranking and performance deviation</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The majority of the analysis is performed in HiveQL and visualized in Apache Zeppelin.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785018959281_1309669631","id":"paragraph_1785018959281_1309669631","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:35:59+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:38:12+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:38:12+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nDROP VIEW IF EXISTS retail_events_analytics;\n\nCREATE VIEW retail_events_analytics AS\nSELECT\n    row_key,\n    transaction_id,\n    CAST(event_timestamp AS TIMESTAMP) AS event_timestamp,\n    payment_type,\n    loyalty_flag,\n    product_id,\n    product_name,\n    category,\n    store_id,\n    store_city,\n    province,\n    store_region,\n    CAST(quantity AS INT) AS quantity,\n    CAST(unit_price AS DECIMAL(10,2)) AS unit_price,\n    CAST(discount_amount AS DECIMAL(10,2)) AS discount_amount,\n    CAST(final_price AS DECIMAL(10,2)) AS final_price,\n    promotion_flag\nFROM retail_events_hive;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:38:23+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"Query executed successfully. Affected rows : 0\n\n"},{"type":"TEXT","data":"Query executed successfully. Affected rows : 0\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785019092540_4057812","id":"paragraph_1785019092540_4057812","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:38:12+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:38:23+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:38:23+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nSELECT\n    row_key,\n    transaction_id,\n    event_timestamp,\n    store_id,\n    quantity,\n    final_price\nFROM retail_events_analytics\nLIMIT 10;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:38:35+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TABLE","data":"row_key\ttransaction_id\tevent_timestamp\tstore_id\tquantity\tfinal_price\nST-BRA-001#9223370252001614807#EVT-00037948\tTXN-0012661\t2026-07-23 20:32:41.0\tST-BRA-001\t1\t3.26\nST-BRA-001#9223370252001614807#EVT-00037949\tTXN-0012661\t2026-07-23 20:32:41.0\tST-BRA-001\t1\t13.09\nST-BRA-001#9223370252001614807#EVT-00037950\tTXN-0012661\t2026-07-23 20:32:41.0\tST-BRA-001\t2\t9.78\nST-BRA-001#9223370252002399807#EVT-00037942\tTXN-0012659\t2026-07-23 20:19:36.0\tST-BRA-001\t2\t27.92\nST-BRA-001#9223370252002399807#EVT-00037943\tTXN-0012659\t2026-07-23 20:19:36.0\tST-BRA-001\t1\t3.23\nST-BRA-001#9223370252004418807#EVT-00037938\tTXN-0012658\t2026-07-23 19:45:57.0\tST-BRA-001\t1\t14.77\nST-BRA-001#9223370252004418807#EVT-00037939\tTXN-0012658\t2026-07-23 19:45:57.0\tST-BRA-001\t1\t14.91\nST-BRA-001#9223370252004418807#EVT-00037940\tTXN-0012658\t2026-07-23 19:45:57.0\tST-BRA-001\t1\t7.20\nST-BRA-001#9223370252004418807#EVT-00037941\tTXN-0012658\t2026-07-23 19:45:57.0\tST-BRA-001\t1\t15.30\nST-BRA-001#9223370252006385807#EVT-00037954\tTXN-0012663\t2026-07-23 19:13:10.0\tST-BRA-001\t1\t3.09\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785019103432_2106990620","id":"paragraph_1785019103432_2106990620","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:38:23+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:38:35+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:38:36+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nDESCRIBE retail_events_analytics;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:38:56+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TABLE","data":"col_name\tdata_type\tcomment\nrow_key\tstring\t\ntransaction_id\tstring\t\nevent_timestamp\ttimestamp\t\npayment_type\tstring\t\nloyalty_flag\tstring\t\nproduct_id\tstring\t\nproduct_name\tstring\t\ncategory\tstring\t\nstore_id\tstring\t\nstore_city\tstring\t\nprovince\tstring\t\nstore_region\tstring\t\nquantity\tint\t\nunit_price\tdecimal(10,2)\t\ndiscount_amount\tdecimal(10,2)\t\nfinal_price\tdecimal(10,2)\t\npromotion_flag\tstring\t\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785019115929_1238899477","id":"paragraph_1785019115929_1238899477","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:38:35+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:38:56+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:38:56+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n### Analytical View Validation\n\nThe `retail_events_analytics` view converts the HBase-backed string values into appropriate analytical data types.\n\nThe timestamp field is converted to `TIMESTAMP`, quantity is converted to `INT`, and monetary values are converted to `DECIMAL`.\n\nThis typed view simplifies the remaining HiveQL queries and reduces the need to repeatedly cast fields during advanced analysis.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:40:06+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Analytical View Validation</h3>\n<p>The <code>retail_events_analytics</code> view converts the HBase-backed string values into appropriate analytical data types.</p>\n<p>The timestamp field is converted to <code>TIMESTAMP</code>, quantity is converted to <code>INT</code>, and monetary values are converted to <code>DECIMAL</code>.</p>\n<p>This typed view simplifies the remaining HiveQL queries and reduces the need to repeatedly cast fields during advanced analysis.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785019136341_1963530007","id":"paragraph_1785019136341_1963530007","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:38:56+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:40:06+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:40:06+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n## 2. Transaction-Level Analytics\n\n### Business Question\n\nWhat is the value and size of each customer transaction, and how does transaction performance vary across stores?\n\n### Analysis Method\n\nThe original dataset stores one row for each retail product event. Therefore, multiple rows may belong to the same transaction.\n\nThis analysis groups records by `transaction_id` to calculate:\n\n- Total transaction value\n- Total quantity purchased\n- Number of distinct products\n- Number of product lines\n- Store-level transaction count\n- Average transaction value by store\n\nThis transaction-level view provides a more accurate measurement of customer spending behavior.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:45:24+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>2. Transaction-Level Analytics</h2>\n<h3>Business Question</h3>\n<p>What is the value and size of each customer transaction, and how does transaction performance vary across stores?</p>\n<h3>Analysis Method</h3>\n<p>The original dataset stores one row for each retail product event. Therefore, multiple rows may belong to the same transaction.</p>\n<p>This analysis groups records by <code>transaction_id</code> to calculate:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Total transaction value</li>\n<li>Total quantity purchased</li>\n<li>Number of distinct products</li>\n<li>Number of product lines</li>\n<li>Store-level transaction count</li>\n<li>Average transaction value by store</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This transaction-level view provides a more accurate measurement of customer spending behavior.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785019206667_1966131022","id":"paragraph_1785019206667_1966131022","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:40:06+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:45:24+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:45:24+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nDROP VIEW IF EXISTS transaction_summary;\n\nCREATE VIEW transaction_summary AS\nSELECT\n    transaction_id,\n    store_id,\n    store_city,\n    province,\n    store_region,\n    payment_type,\n    loyalty_flag,\n    MIN(event_timestamp) AS transaction_timestamp,\n    COUNT(*) AS product_lines,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT product_id) AS distinct_products,\n    SUM(quantity) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(final_price), 2) AS transaction_value\nFROM retail_events_analytics\nGROUP BY\n    transaction_id,\n    store_id,\n    store_city,\n    province,\n    store_region,\n    payment_type,\n    loyalty_flag;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:45:38+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"Query executed successfully. Affected rows : 0\n\n"},{"type":"TEXT","data":"Query executed successfully. Affected rows : 0\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785019524691_1893205992","id":"paragraph_1785019524691_1893205992","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:45:24+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:45:38+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:45:38+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nSELECT\n    transaction_id,\n    store_id,\n    product_lines,\n    distinct_products,\n    total_quantity,\n    transaction_value\nFROM transaction_summary\nORDER BY transaction_value DESC\nLIMIT 10;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:45:58+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"INFO  : Compiling command(queryId=root_20260725224558_e0c6d42b-c2ab-421b-be06-08c707752793): \n\nSELECT\n    transaction_id,\n    store_id,\n    product_lines,\n    distinct_products,\n    total_quantity,\n    transaction_value\nFROM transaction_summary\nORDER BY transaction_value DESC\nLIMIT 10\nINFO  : No Stats for default@retail_events_hive, Columns: transaction_id, store_id, payment_type, store_city, loyalty_flag, quantity, province, final_price, product_id, event_timestamp, store_region\nINFO  : Semantic Analysis Completed (retrial = false)\nINFO  : Created Hive schema: Schema(fieldSchemas:[FieldSchema(name:transaction_id, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:store_id, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:product_lines, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:distinct_products, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_quantity, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:transaction_value, type:decimal(20,2), comment:null)], properties:null)\nINFO  : Completed compiling command(queryId=root_20260725224558_e0c6d42b-c2ab-421b-be06-08c707752793); Time taken: 0.154 seconds\nINFO  : Concurrency mode is disabled, not creating a lock manager\nINFO  : Executing command(queryId=root_20260725224558_e0c6d42b-c2ab-421b-be06-08c707752793): \n\nSELECT\n    transaction_id,\n    store_id,\n    product_lines,\n    distinct_products,\n    total_quantity,\n    transaction_value\nFROM transaction_summary\nORDER BY transaction_value DESC\nLIMIT 10\nWARN  : Hive-on-MR is deprecated in Hive 2 and may not be available in the future versions. Consider using a different execution engine (i.e. tez) or using Hive 1.X releases.\nINFO  : Query ID = root_20260725224558_e0c6d42b-c2ab-421b-be06-08c707752793\nINFO  : Total jobs = 2\nINFO  : Launching Job 1 out of 2\nINFO  : Starting task [Stage-1:MAPRED] in serial mode\nINFO  : Number of reduce tasks not specified. Estimated from input data size: 1\nINFO  : In order to change the average load for a reducer (in bytes):\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.bytes.per.reducer=<number>\nINFO  : In order to limit the maximum number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.max=<number>\nINFO  : In order to set a constant number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set mapreduce.job.reduces=<number>\n"},{"type":"TABLE","data":"transaction_id\tstore_id\tproduct_lines\tdistinct_products\ttotal_quantity\ttransaction_value\nTXN-0011541\tST-CAL-001\t7\t7\t18\t201.09\nTXN-0002111\tST-CAL-001\t6\t6\t16\t198.15\nTXN-0011935\tST-KIT-001\t7\t7\t18\t186.00\nTXN-0006509\tST-SCA-001\t7\t7\t16\t183.16\nTXN-0009967\tST-OTT-001\t7\t7\t14\t180.63\nTXN-0007039\tST-KIT-001\t7\t7\t15\t179.64\nTXN-0008925\tST-OTT-001\t7\t7\t14\t173.72\nTXN-0008736\tST-KIT-001\t7\t7\t15\t172.97\nTXN-0001950\tST-CAL-001\t6\t6\t14\t172.62\nTXN-0001516\tST-EDM-001\t7\t7\t17\t169.82\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785019538141_164525988","id":"paragraph_1785019538141_164525988","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:45:38+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:45:58+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:46:39+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS total_transactions\nFROM transaction_summary;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:46:46+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"INFO  : Compiling command(queryId=root_20260725224646_f7a82138-b9d1-4532-933c-b2f33cdde0ae): \n\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS total_transactions\nFROM transaction_summary\nINFO  : No Stats for default@retail_events_hive, Columns: transaction_id, store_id, payment_type, store_city, loyalty_flag, quantity, province, final_price, product_id, event_timestamp, store_region\nINFO  : Semantic Analysis Completed (retrial = false)\nINFO  : Created Hive schema: Schema(fieldSchemas:[FieldSchema(name:total_transactions, type:bigint, comment:null)], properties:null)\nINFO  : Completed compiling command(queryId=root_20260725224646_f7a82138-b9d1-4532-933c-b2f33cdde0ae); Time taken: 0.127 seconds\nINFO  : Concurrency mode is disabled, not creating a lock manager\nINFO  : Executing command(queryId=root_20260725224646_f7a82138-b9d1-4532-933c-b2f33cdde0ae): \n\nSELECT COUNT(*) AS total_transactions\nFROM transaction_summary\nWARN  : Hive-on-MR is deprecated in Hive 2 and may not be available in the future versions. Consider using a different execution engine (i.e. tez) or using Hive 1.X releases.\nINFO  : Query ID = root_20260725224646_f7a82138-b9d1-4532-933c-b2f33cdde0ae\nINFO  : Total jobs = 2\nINFO  : Launching Job 1 out of 2\nINFO  : Starting task [Stage-1:MAPRED] in serial mode\nINFO  : Number of reduce tasks not specified. Estimated from input data size: 1\nINFO  : In order to change the average load for a reducer (in bytes):\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.bytes.per.reducer=<number>\nINFO  : In order to limit the maximum number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.max=<number>\nINFO  : In order to set a constant number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set mapreduce.job.reduces=<number>\n"},{"type":"TABLE","data":"total_transactions\n12725\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785019558335_235095158","id":"paragraph_1785019558335_235095158","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:45:58+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:46:46+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:47:22+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n### Transaction Summary Validation\n\nThe `transaction_summary` view combines multiple product-level records into one transaction-level record.\n\nThe view contains **12,725 transactions**, matching the previously validated number of distinct transaction IDs.\n\nEach row now represents one complete customer transaction and includes its total value, total quantity, product-line count, and number of distinct products.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:47:43+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Transaction Summary Validation</h3>\n<p>The <code>transaction_summary</code> view combines multiple product-level records into one transaction-level record.</p>\n<p>The view contains <strong>12,725 transactions</strong>, matching the previously validated number of distinct transaction IDs.</p>\n<p>Each row now represents one complete customer transaction and includes its total value, total quantity, product-line count, and number of distinct products.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785019606078_18746224","id":"paragraph_1785019606078_18746224","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:46:46+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:47:43+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:47:43+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nSELECT\n    COUNT(*) AS total_transactions,\n    ROUND(SUM(transaction_value), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(transaction_value), 2) AS average_transaction_value,\n    ROUND(MIN(transaction_value), 2) AS minimum_transaction_value,\n    ROUND(MAX(transaction_value), 2) AS maximum_transaction_value,\n    ROUND(AVG(total_quantity), 2) AS average_quantity_per_transaction,\n    ROUND(AVG(distinct_products), 2) AS average_products_per_transaction\nFROM transaction_summary;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:58:04+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{"1":{"graph":{"mode":"table","height":300,"optionOpen":false,"setting":{"multiBarChart":{"rotate":{"degree":"-45"},"xLabelStatus":"default","stacked":false}},"keys":[{"name":"total_transactions","index":0,"aggr":"sum"}],"groups":[],"values":[{"name":"total_revenue","index":1,"aggr":"sum"}]}}},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"INFO  : Compiling command(queryId=root_20260725224753_40912bd6-a5a2-4aad-b8e3-5cec8d953bb9): \n\nSELECT\n    COUNT(*) AS total_transactions,\n    ROUND(SUM(transaction_value), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(transaction_value), 2) AS average_transaction_value,\n    ROUND(MIN(transaction_value), 2) AS minimum_transaction_value,\n    ROUND(MAX(transaction_value), 2) AS maximum_transaction_value,\n    ROUND(AVG(total_quantity), 2) AS average_quantity_per_transaction,\n    ROUND(AVG(distinct_products), 2) AS average_products_per_transaction\nFROM transaction_summary\nINFO  : No Stats for default@retail_events_hive, Columns: transaction_id, store_id, payment_type, store_city, loyalty_flag, quantity, province, final_price, product_id, event_timestamp, store_region\nINFO  : Semantic Analysis Completed (retrial = false)\nINFO  : Created Hive schema: Schema(fieldSchemas:[FieldSchema(name:total_transactions, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_revenue, type:decimal(30,2), comment:null), FieldSchema(name:average_transaction_value, type:decimal(21,2), comment:null), FieldSchema(name:minimum_transaction_value, type:decimal(20,2), comment:null), FieldSchema(name:maximum_transaction_value, type:decimal(20,2), comment:null), FieldSchema(name:average_quantity_per_transaction, type:double, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:average_products_per_transaction, type:double, comment:null)], properties:null)\nINFO  : Completed compiling command(queryId=root_20260725224753_40912bd6-a5a2-4aad-b8e3-5cec8d953bb9); Time taken: 0.15 seconds\nINFO  : Concurrency mode is disabled, not creating a lock manager\nINFO  : Executing command(queryId=root_20260725224753_40912bd6-a5a2-4aad-b8e3-5cec8d953bb9): \n\nSELECT\n    COUNT(*) AS total_transactions,\n    ROUND(SUM(transaction_value), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(transaction_value), 2) AS average_transaction_value,\n    ROUND(MIN(transaction_value), 2) AS minimum_transaction_value,\n    ROUND(MAX(transaction_value), 2) AS maximum_transaction_value,\n    ROUND(AVG(total_quantity), 2) AS average_quantity_per_transaction,\n    ROUND(AVG(distinct_products), 2) AS average_products_per_transaction\nFROM transaction_summary\nWARN  : Hive-on-MR is deprecated in Hive 2 and may not be available in the future versions. Consider using a different execution engine (i.e. tez) or using Hive 1.X releases.\nINFO  : Query ID = root_20260725224753_40912bd6-a5a2-4aad-b8e3-5cec8d953bb9\nINFO  : Total jobs = 2\nINFO  : Launching Job 1 out of 2\nINFO  : Starting task [Stage-1:MAPRED] in serial mode\nINFO  : Number of reduce tasks not specified. Estimated from input data size: 1\nINFO  : In order to change the average load for a reducer (in bytes):\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.bytes.per.reducer=<number>\nINFO  : In order to limit the maximum number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.max=<number>\nINFO  : In order to set a constant number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set mapreduce.job.reduces=<number>\n"},{"type":"TABLE","data":"total_transactions\ttotal_revenue\taverage_transaction_value\tminimum_transaction_value\tmaximum_transaction_value\taverage_quantity_per_transaction\taverage_products_per_transaction\n12725\t539730.95\t42.42\t1.85\t201.09\t4.63\t3.0\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785019663390_1322773379","id":"paragraph_1785019663390_1322773379","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:47:43+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:47:53+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:48:33+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n### Overall Transaction Performance\n\nThe dataset contains **12,725 completed transactions**.\n\nThe average transaction value is approximately **$42.42**, while the highest transaction value is approximately **$201.09**.\n\nOn average, each transaction contains **4.63** units and **3.0** distinct products.\n\nThese results provide a transaction-level view of customer spending and basket size.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:50:07+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Overall Transaction Performance</h3>\n<p>The dataset contains <strong>12,725 completed transactions</strong>.</p>\n<p>The average transaction value is approximately <strong>$42.42</strong>, while the highest transaction value is approximately <strong>$201.09</strong>.</p>\n<p>On average, each transaction contains <strong>4.63</strong> units and <strong>3.0</strong> distinct products.</p>\n<p>These results provide a transaction-level view of customer spending and basket size.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785019673890_69925518","id":"paragraph_1785019673890_69925518","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:47:53+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:50:07+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:50:07+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n### Transaction Performance by Store\n\nThis query compares store performance using transaction-level metrics rather than individual product-event records.\n\nThe analysis includes:\n\n- Number of distinct transactions\n- Total revenue\n- Average transaction value\n- Average quantity per transaction\n- Average number of products per transaction","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:51:16+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Transaction Performance by Store</h3>\n<p>This query compares store performance using transaction-level metrics rather than individual product-event records.</p>\n<p>The analysis includes:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Number of distinct transactions</li>\n<li>Total revenue</li>\n<li>Average transaction value</li>\n<li>Average quantity per transaction</li>\n<li>Average number of products per transaction</li>\n</ul>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785019807788_789756810","id":"paragraph_1785019807788_789756810","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:50:07+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:51:16+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:51:16+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nSELECT\n    store_id,\n    store_city,\n    store_region,\n    COUNT(*) AS total_transactions,\n    ROUND(SUM(transaction_value), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(transaction_value), 2) AS average_transaction_value,\n    ROUND(AVG(total_quantity), 2) AS average_quantity_per_transaction,\n    ROUND(AVG(distinct_products), 2) AS average_products_per_transaction\nFROM transaction_summary\nGROUP BY\n    store_id,\n    store_city,\n    store_region\nORDER BY average_transaction_value DESC;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:59:47+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{"1":{"graph":{"mode":"table","height":300,"optionOpen":true,"setting":{"multiBarChart":{"rotate":{"degree":"-45"},"xLabelStatus":"default","stacked":false}},"keys":[{"name":"store_id","index":0,"aggr":"sum"}],"groups":[],"values":[{"name":"average_transaction_value","index":5,"aggr":"sum"}]}}},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"INFO  : Compiling command(queryId=root_20260725225127_fc232b02-3fb0-43f1-ba4d-63d6ded4fa03): \n\nSELECT\n    store_id,\n    store_city,\n    store_region,\n    COUNT(*) AS total_transactions,\n    ROUND(SUM(transaction_value), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(transaction_value), 2) AS average_transaction_value,\n    ROUND(AVG(total_quantity), 2) AS average_quantity_per_transaction,\n    ROUND(AVG(distinct_products), 2) AS average_products_per_transaction\nFROM transaction_summary\nGROUP BY\n    store_id,\n    store_city,\n    store_region\nORDER BY average_transaction_value DESC\nINFO  : No Stats for default@retail_events_hive, Columns: transaction_id, store_id, payment_type, store_city, loyalty_flag, quantity, province, final_price, product_id, event_timestamp, store_region\nINFO  : Semantic Analysis Completed (retrial = false)\nINFO  : Created Hive schema: Schema(fieldSchemas:[FieldSchema(name:store_id, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:store_city, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:store_region, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_transactions, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_revenue, type:decimal(30,2), comment:null), FieldSchema(name:average_transaction_value, type:decimal(21,2), comment:null), FieldSchema(name:average_quantity_per_transaction, type:double, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:average_products_per_transaction, type:double, comment:null)], properties:null)\nINFO  : Completed compiling command(queryId=root_20260725225127_fc232b02-3fb0-43f1-ba4d-63d6ded4fa03); Time taken: 0.156 seconds\nINFO  : Concurrency mode is disabled, not creating a lock manager\nINFO  : Executing command(queryId=root_20260725225127_fc232b02-3fb0-43f1-ba4d-63d6ded4fa03): \n\nSELECT\n    store_id,\n    store_city,\n    store_region,\n    COUNT(*) AS total_transactions,\n    ROUND(SUM(transaction_value), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(transaction_value), 2) AS average_transaction_value,\n    ROUND(AVG(total_quantity), 2) AS average_quantity_per_transaction,\n    ROUND(AVG(distinct_products), 2) AS average_products_per_transaction\nFROM transaction_summary\nGROUP BY\n    store_id,\n    store_city,\n    store_region\nORDER BY average_transaction_value DESC\nWARN  : Hive-on-MR is deprecated in Hive 2 and may not be available in the future versions. Consider using a different execution engine (i.e. tez) or using Hive 1.X releases.\nINFO  : Query ID = root_20260725225127_fc232b02-3fb0-43f1-ba4d-63d6ded4fa03\nINFO  : Total jobs = 2\nINFO  : Launching Job 1 out of 2\nINFO  : Starting task [Stage-1:MAPRED] in serial mode\nINFO  : Number of reduce tasks not specified. Estimated from input data size: 1\nINFO  : In order to change the average load for a reducer (in bytes):\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.bytes.per.reducer=<number>\nINFO  : In order to limit the maximum number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.max=<number>\nINFO  : In order to set a constant number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set mapreduce.job.reduces=<number>\n"},{"type":"TABLE","data":"store_id\tstore_city\tstore_region\ttotal_transactions\ttotal_revenue\taverage_transaction_value\taverage_quantity_per_transaction\taverage_products_per_transaction\nST-CAL-001\tCalgary\tWestern\t1167\t55573.77\t47.62\t5.18\t2.96\nST-TOR-002\tToronto\tCentral\t1151\t49425.30\t42.94\t4.62\t3.04\nST-OTT-002\tOttawa\tEastern\t940\t40078.66\t42.64\t4.67\t3.05\nST-HAM-001\tHamilton\tCentral\t939\t39916.22\t42.51\t4.63\t3.01\nST-SCA-001\tScarborough\tCentral\t949\t40277.22\t42.44\t4.66\t3.03\nST-EDM-001\tEdmonton\tWestern\t1094\t46308.45\t42.33\t4.62\t3.02\nST-LON-001\tLondon\tCentral\t947\t40069.41\t42.31\t4.53\t2.97\nST-OTT-001\tOttawa\tEastern\t1157\t48425.04\t41.85\t4.61\t3.04\nST-TOR-001\tToronto\tCentral\t1302\t54080.88\t41.54\t4.53\t2.96\nST-KIT-001\tKitchener\tCentral\t921\t37874.89\t41.12\t4.5\t3.02\nST-MIS-001\tMississauga\tCentral\t1154\t47075.34\t40.79\t4.54\t2.96\nST-BRA-001\tBrampton\tCentral\t1004\t40625.77\t40.46\t4.43\t2.92\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785019876345_1692066361","id":"paragraph_1785019876345_1692066361","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:51:16+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:51:27+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:52:02+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n### Interpretation\n\nStore **ST-CAL-001** recorded the highest average transaction value at approximately **$47.62**.\n\nThe store completed **1167** transactions and generated approximately **$55,573.77** in total revenue.\n\nA high average transaction value indicates that customers at this location spend more per visit. However, this result should be considered together with total transaction volume because a store may have a high average transaction value but relatively few transactions.\n\nManagement should evaluate both customer traffic and average basket value when comparing store performance.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-25T22:55:32+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Interpretation</h3>\n<p>Store <strong>ST-CAL-001</strong> recorded the highest average transaction value at approximately <strong>$47.62</strong>.</p>\n<p>The store completed <strong>1167</strong> transactions and generated approximately <strong>$55,573.77</strong> in total revenue.</p>\n<p>A high average transaction value indicates that customers at this location spend more per visit. However, this result should be considered together with total transaction volume because a store may have a high average transaction value but relatively few transactions.</p>\n<p>Management should evaluate both customer traffic and average basket value when comparing store performance.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785019887480_1610236201","id":"paragraph_1785019887480_1610236201","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:51:27+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-25T22:55:32+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-25T22:55:32+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n## 3. Regional Performance Analysis\n\n### Business Question\n\nHow does retail performance vary across different regions?\n\n### Analysis Method\n\nThis analysis groups transaction-level records by region and calculates:\n\n- Number of stores\n- Number of transactions\n- Total quantity purchased\n- Total revenue\n- Average transaction value\n- Average revenue per store\n\nThe results help identify the strongest and weakest regional markets while accounting for differences in the number of store locations.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T16:24:21+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"enabled":true,"results":{},"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"editorHide":true,"tableHide":false},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>3. Regional Performance Analysis</h2>\n<h3>Business Question</h3>\n<p>How does retail performance vary across different regions?</p>\n<h3>Analysis Method</h3>\n<p>This analysis groups transaction-level records by region and calculates:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Number of stores</li>\n<li>Number of transactions</li>\n<li>Total quantity purchased</li>\n<li>Total revenue</li>\n<li>Average transaction value</li>\n<li>Average revenue per store</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The results help identify the strongest and weakest regional markets while accounting for differences in the number of store locations.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785020132213_1329946949","id":"paragraph_1785020132213_1329946949","dateCreated":"2026-07-25T22:55:32+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T16:24:21+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T16:24:22+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nSELECT\n    store_region,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT store_id) AS total_stores,\n    COUNT(*) AS total_transactions,\n    SUM(total_quantity) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(transaction_value), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(transaction_value), 2) AS average_transaction_value,\n    ROUND(\n        SUM(transaction_value) / COUNT(DISTINCT store_id),\n        2\n    ) AS average_revenue_per_store\nFROM transaction_summary\nGROUP BY store_region\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T16:32:30+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{"1":{"graph":{"mode":"multiBarChart","height":300,"optionOpen":true,"setting":{"multiBarChart":{"rotate":{"degree":"-45"},"xLabelStatus":"default","stacked":false}},"keys":[{"name":"store_region","index":0,"aggr":"sum"}],"groups":[],"values":[{"name":"total_revenue","index":4,"aggr":"sum"}]}}},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"INFO  : Compiling command(queryId=root_20260726162505_d871afc1-4121-4242-9d9d-ca7d68b8162b): \n\nSELECT\n    store_region,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT store_id) AS total_stores,\n    COUNT(*) AS total_transactions,\n    SUM(total_quantity) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(transaction_value), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(transaction_value), 2) AS average_transaction_value,\n    ROUND(\n        SUM(transaction_value) / COUNT(DISTINCT store_id),\n        2\n    ) AS average_revenue_per_store\nFROM transaction_summary\nGROUP BY store_region\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC\nINFO  : No Stats for default@retail_events_hive, Columns: transaction_id, store_id, payment_type, store_city, loyalty_flag, quantity, province, final_price, product_id, event_timestamp, store_region\nINFO  : Semantic Analysis Completed (retrial = false)\nINFO  : Created Hive schema: Schema(fieldSchemas:[FieldSchema(name:store_region, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_stores, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_transactions, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_quantity, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_revenue, type:decimal(30,2), comment:null), FieldSchema(name:average_transaction_value, type:decimal(21,2), comment:null), FieldSchema(name:average_revenue_per_store, type:decimal(31,2), comment:null)], properties:null)\nINFO  : Completed compiling command(queryId=root_20260726162505_d871afc1-4121-4242-9d9d-ca7d68b8162b); Time taken: 0.255 seconds\nINFO  : Concurrency mode is disabled, not creating a lock manager\nINFO  : Executing command(queryId=root_20260726162505_d871afc1-4121-4242-9d9d-ca7d68b8162b): \n\nSELECT\n    store_region,\n    COUNT(DISTINCT store_id) AS total_stores,\n    COUNT(*) AS total_transactions,\n    SUM(total_quantity) AS total_quantity,\n    ROUND(SUM(transaction_value), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(transaction_value), 2) AS average_transaction_value,\n    ROUND(\n        SUM(transaction_value) / COUNT(DISTINCT store_id),\n        2\n    ) AS average_revenue_per_store\nFROM transaction_summary\nGROUP BY store_region\nORDER BY total_revenue DESC\nWARN  : Hive-on-MR is deprecated in Hive 2 and may not be available in the future versions. Consider using a different execution engine (i.e. tez) or using Hive 1.X releases.\nINFO  : Query ID = root_20260726162505_d871afc1-4121-4242-9d9d-ca7d68b8162b\nINFO  : Total jobs = 3\nINFO  : Launching Job 1 out of 3\nINFO  : Starting task [Stage-1:MAPRED] in serial mode\nINFO  : Number of reduce tasks not specified. Estimated from input data size: 1\nINFO  : In order to change the average load for a reducer (in bytes):\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.bytes.per.reducer=<number>\nINFO  : In order to limit the maximum number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.max=<number>\nINFO  : In order to set a constant number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set mapreduce.job.reduces=<number>\n"},{"type":"TABLE","data":"store_region\ttotal_stores\ttotal_transactions\ttotal_quantity\ttotal_revenue\taverage_transaction_value\taverage_revenue_per_store\nCentral\t8\t8367\t38114\t349345.03\t41.75\t43668.13\nWestern\t2\t2261\t11102\t101882.22\t45.06\t50941.11\nEastern\t2\t2097\t9720\t88503.70\t42.20\t44251.85\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785083061232_1169757760","id":"paragraph_1785083061232_1169757760","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T16:24:21+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T16:25:04+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T16:26:01+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n### Regional Revenue Interpretation\n\nThe **Central** region generated the highest total revenue, reaching approximately **$349,345.03**.\n\nThe region includes **8** stores and completed **8367** transactions. Its average transaction value was approximately **$41.75**.\n\nAlthough total revenue measures the region's overall contribution, the number of stores must also be considered. A region with more stores may naturally generate more revenue.\n\nFor this reason, average revenue per store provides an additional measure for comparing the operating performance of regions with different store counts.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T16:32:21+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Regional Revenue Interpretation</h3>\n<p>The <strong>Central</strong> region generated the highest total revenue, reaching approximately <strong>$349,345.03</strong>.</p>\n<p>The region includes <strong>8</strong> stores and completed <strong>8367</strong> transactions. Its average transaction value was approximately <strong>$41.75</strong>.</p>\n<p>Although total revenue measures the region&rsquo;s overall contribution, the number of stores must also be considered. A region with more stores may naturally generate more revenue.</p>\n<p>For this reason, average revenue per store provides an additional measure for comparing the operating performance of regions with different store counts.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785083104373_316380041","id":"paragraph_1785083104373_316380041","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T16:25:04+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T16:32:21+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T16:32:21+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n### Sales per Store by Region\n\nTotal regional revenue can be influenced by the number of stores operating in each region.\n\nThe following analysis calculates average revenue per store to provide a fairer comparison of regional performance.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T16:35:12+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Sales per Store by Region</h3>\n<p>Total regional revenue can be influenced by the number of stores operating in each region.</p>\n<p>The following analysis calculates average revenue per store to provide a fairer comparison of regional performance.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785083541917_1165646294","id":"paragraph_1785083541917_1165646294","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T16:32:21+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T16:35:12+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T16:35:12+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nWITH store_performance AS (\n    SELECT\n        store_region,\n        store_id,\n        COUNT(*) AS total_transactions,\n        ROUND(SUM(transaction_value), 2) AS store_revenue,\n        ROUND(AVG(transaction_value), 2) AS average_transaction_value\n    FROM transaction_summary\n    GROUP BY\n        store_region,\n        store_id\n)\n\nSELECT\n    store_region,\n    COUNT(*) AS total_stores,\n    SUM(total_transactions) AS total_transactions,\n    ROUND(SUM(store_revenue), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(store_revenue), 2) AS average_revenue_per_store,\n    ROUND(AVG(average_transaction_value), 2)\n        AS average_transaction_value\nFROM store_performance\nGROUP BY store_region\nORDER BY average_revenue_per_store DESC;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T16:51:45+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{"1":{"graph":{"mode":"multiBarChart","height":626.2083435058594,"optionOpen":true,"setting":{"multiBarChart":{"rotate":{"degree":"-45"},"xLabelStatus":"default","stacked":false}},"keys":[{"name":"store_region","index":0,"aggr":"sum"}],"groups":[],"values":[{"name":"average_revenue_per_store","index":4,"aggr":"sum"}]}}},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"INFO  : Compiling command(queryId=root_20260726163539_09d2820d-3836-4593-a348-9d4630350fe0): \n\nWITH store_performance AS (\n    SELECT\n        store_region,\n        store_id,\n        COUNT(*) AS total_transactions,\n        ROUND(SUM(transaction_value), 2) AS store_revenue,\n        ROUND(AVG(transaction_value), 2) AS average_transaction_value\n    FROM transaction_summary\n    GROUP BY\n        store_region,\n        store_id\n)\n\nSELECT\n    store_region,\n    COUNT(*) AS total_stores,\n    SUM(total_transactions) AS total_transactions,\n    ROUND(SUM(store_revenue), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(store_revenue), 2) AS average_revenue_per_store,\n    ROUND(AVG(average_transaction_value), 2)\n        AS average_transaction_value\nFROM store_performance\nGROUP BY store_region\nORDER BY average_revenue_per_store DESC\nINFO  : No Stats for default@retail_events_hive, Columns: transaction_id, store_id, payment_type, store_city, loyalty_flag, quantity, province, final_price, product_id, event_timestamp, store_region\nINFO  : Semantic Analysis Completed (retrial = false)\nINFO  : Created Hive schema: Schema(fieldSchemas:[FieldSchema(name:store_region, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_stores, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_transactions, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_revenue, type:decimal(38,2), comment:null), FieldSchema(name:average_revenue_per_store, type:decimal(31,2), comment:null), FieldSchema(name:average_transaction_value, type:decimal(22,2), comment:null)], properties:null)\nINFO  : Completed compiling command(queryId=root_20260726163539_09d2820d-3836-4593-a348-9d4630350fe0); Time taken: 0.201 seconds\nINFO  : Concurrency mode is disabled, not creating a lock manager\nINFO  : Executing command(queryId=root_20260726163539_09d2820d-3836-4593-a348-9d4630350fe0): \n\nWITH store_performance AS (\n    SELECT\n        store_region,\n        store_id,\n        COUNT(*) AS total_transactions,\n        ROUND(SUM(transaction_value), 2) AS store_revenue,\n        ROUND(AVG(transaction_value), 2) AS average_transaction_value\n    FROM transaction_summary\n    GROUP BY\n        store_region,\n        store_id\n)\n\nSELECT\n    store_region,\n    COUNT(*) AS total_stores,\n    SUM(total_transactions) AS total_transactions,\n    ROUND(SUM(store_revenue), 2) AS total_revenue,\n    ROUND(AVG(store_revenue), 2) AS average_revenue_per_store,\n    ROUND(AVG(average_transaction_value), 2)\n        AS average_transaction_value\nFROM store_performance\nGROUP BY store_region\nORDER BY average_revenue_per_store DESC\nWARN  : Hive-on-MR is deprecated in Hive 2 and may not be available in the future versions. Consider using a different execution engine (i.e. tez) or using Hive 1.X releases.\nINFO  : Query ID = root_20260726163539_09d2820d-3836-4593-a348-9d4630350fe0\nINFO  : Total jobs = 2\nINFO  : Launching Job 1 out of 2\nINFO  : Starting task [Stage-1:MAPRED] in serial mode\nINFO  : Number of reduce tasks not specified. Estimated from input data size: 1\nINFO  : In order to change the average load for a reducer (in bytes):\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.bytes.per.reducer=<number>\nINFO  : In order to limit the maximum number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.max=<number>\nINFO  : In order to set a constant number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set mapreduce.job.reduces=<number>\n"},{"type":"TABLE","data":"store_region\ttotal_stores\ttotal_transactions\ttotal_revenue\taverage_revenue_per_store\taverage_transaction_value\nWestern\t2\t2261\t101882.22\t50941.11\t44.98\nEastern\t2\t2097\t88503.70\t44251.85\t42.25\nCentral\t8\t8367\t349345.03\t43668.13\t41.76\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785083712183_1559679984","id":"paragraph_1785083712183_1559679984","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T16:35:12+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T16:35:39+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T16:36:20+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n### Sales per Store Interpretation\n\nThe **Western** region recorded the highest average revenue per store at approximately **$50,941.11**.\n\nThis result indicates that its individual store locations performed strongly, even after controlling for differences in the number of stores across regions.\n\nA region may rank highly in total revenue because it has many stores, while another region may demonstrate stronger store-level efficiency.\n\nManagement should therefore consider both total regional revenue and average revenue per store when making decisions about store expansion, staffing, and inventory allocation.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T16:37:49+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Sales per Store Interpretation</h3>\n<p>The <strong>Western</strong> region recorded the highest average revenue per store at approximately <strong>$50,941.11</strong>.</p>\n<p>This result indicates that its individual store locations performed strongly, even after controlling for differences in the number of stores across regions.</p>\n<p>A region may rank highly in total revenue because it has many stores, while another region may demonstrate stronger store-level efficiency.</p>\n<p>Management should therefore consider both total regional revenue and average revenue per store when making decisions about store expansion, staffing, and inventory allocation.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785083739015_2132704710","id":"paragraph_1785083739015_2132704710","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T16:35:39+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T16:37:49+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T16:37:49+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nWITH regional_performance AS (\n    SELECT\n        store_region,\n        COUNT(DISTINCT store_id) AS total_stores,\n        COUNT(*) AS total_transactions,\n        ROUND(SUM(transaction_value), 2) AS total_revenue,\n        ROUND(AVG(transaction_value), 2)\n            AS average_transaction_value\n    FROM transaction_summary\n    GROUP BY store_region\n)\n\nSELECT\n    store_region,\n    total_stores,\n    total_transactions,\n    total_revenue,\n    average_transaction_value,\n    RANK() OVER (\n        ORDER BY total_revenue DESC\n    ) AS revenue_rank\nFROM regional_performance\nORDER BY revenue_rank;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T16:49:46+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{"1":{"graph":{"mode":"table","height":300,"optionOpen":true,"setting":{"multiBarChart":{"rotate":{"degree":"-45"},"xLabelStatus":"default","stacked":false}},"keys":[{"name":"store_region","index":0,"aggr":"sum"}],"groups":[],"values":[{"name":"total_stores","index":1,"aggr":"sum"}]}}},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"INFO  : Compiling command(queryId=root_20260726163839_68b3875d-ec25-4ca9-bce1-9eb18c71f45f): \n\nWITH regional_performance AS (\n    SELECT\n        store_region,\n        COUNT(DISTINCT store_id) AS total_stores,\n        COUNT(*) AS total_transactions,\n        ROUND(SUM(transaction_value), 2) AS total_revenue,\n        ROUND(AVG(transaction_value), 2)\n            AS average_transaction_value\n    FROM transaction_summary\n    GROUP BY store_region\n)\n\nSELECT\n    store_region,\n    total_stores,\n    total_transactions,\n    total_revenue,\n    average_transaction_value,\n    RANK() OVER (\n        ORDER BY total_revenue DESC\n    ) AS revenue_rank\nFROM regional_performance\nORDER BY revenue_rank\nINFO  : No Stats for default@retail_events_hive, Columns: transaction_id, store_id, payment_type, store_city, loyalty_flag, quantity, province, final_price, product_id, event_timestamp, store_region\nINFO  : Semantic Analysis Completed (retrial = false)\nINFO  : Created Hive schema: Schema(fieldSchemas:[FieldSchema(name:store_region, type:string, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_stores, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_transactions, type:bigint, comment:null), FieldSchema(name:total_revenue, type:decimal(30,2), comment:null), FieldSchema(name:average_transaction_value, type:decimal(21,2), comment:null), FieldSchema(name:revenue_rank, type:int, comment:null)], properties:null)\nINFO  : Completed compiling command(queryId=root_20260726163839_68b3875d-ec25-4ca9-bce1-9eb18c71f45f); Time taken: 0.172 seconds\nINFO  : Concurrency mode is disabled, not creating a lock manager\nINFO  : Executing command(queryId=root_20260726163839_68b3875d-ec25-4ca9-bce1-9eb18c71f45f): \n\nWITH regional_performance AS (\n    SELECT\n        store_region,\n        COUNT(DISTINCT store_id) AS total_stores,\n        COUNT(*) AS total_transactions,\n        ROUND(SUM(transaction_value), 2) AS total_revenue,\n        ROUND(AVG(transaction_value), 2)\n            AS average_transaction_value\n    FROM transaction_summary\n    GROUP BY store_region\n)\n\nSELECT\n    store_region,\n    total_stores,\n    total_transactions,\n    total_revenue,\n    average_transaction_value,\n    RANK() OVER (\n        ORDER BY total_revenue DESC\n    ) AS revenue_rank\nFROM regional_performance\nORDER BY revenue_rank\nWARN  : Hive-on-MR is deprecated in Hive 2 and may not be available in the future versions. Consider using a different execution engine (i.e. tez) or using Hive 1.X releases.\nINFO  : Query ID = root_20260726163839_68b3875d-ec25-4ca9-bce1-9eb18c71f45f\nINFO  : Total jobs = 4\nINFO  : Launching Job 1 out of 4\nINFO  : Starting task [Stage-1:MAPRED] in serial mode\nINFO  : Number of reduce tasks not specified. Estimated from input data size: 1\nINFO  : In order to change the average load for a reducer (in bytes):\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.bytes.per.reducer=<number>\nINFO  : In order to limit the maximum number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set hive.exec.reducers.max=<number>\nINFO  : In order to set a constant number of reducers:\nINFO  :   set mapreduce.job.reduces=<number>\n"},{"type":"TABLE","data":"store_region\ttotal_stores\ttotal_transactions\ttotal_revenue\taverage_transaction_value\trevenue_rank\nCentral\t8\t8367\t349345.03\t41.75\t1\nWestern\t2\t2261\t101882.22\t45.06\t2\nEastern\t2\t2097\t88503.70\t42.20\t3\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785083869708_31309808","id":"paragraph_1785083869708_31309808","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T16:37:49+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T16:38:39+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T16:39:54+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n### Regional Ranking\n\nThe ranking query uses the Hive `RANK()` window function to order regions by total revenue.\n\nA revenue rank of **1** represents the highest-performing region based on total revenue.\n\nThe ranking makes regional comparisons easier and demonstrates the use of an advanced HiveQL window function.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T16:40:22+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>Regional Ranking</h3>\n<p>The ranking query uses the Hive <code>RANK()</code> window function to order regions by total revenue.</p>\n<p>A revenue rank of <strong>1</strong> represents the highest-performing region based on total revenue.</p>\n<p>The ranking makes regional comparisons easier and demonstrates the use of an advanced HiveQL window function.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785083919192_1217763791","id":"paragraph_1785083919192_1217763791","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T16:38:39+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T16:40:22+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T16:40:22+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n## 4. Time-Based Activity Analysis","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T16:54:20+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>4. Time-Based Activity Analysis</h2>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785084022376_1020139105","id":"paragraph_1785084022376_1020139105","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T16:40:22+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T16:54:20+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T16:54:20+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n### 4.1 Hourly Transaction Activity\n\n#### Business Question\n\nDuring which hours of the day does the retailer experience the highest transaction activity and revenue?\n\n#### Analysis Method\n\nThe transaction timestamp is used to extract the hour of each transaction.\n\nFor each hour, the analysis calculates:\n\n- Number of transactions\n- Total quantity purchased\n- Total revenue\n- Average transaction value\n\nThis analysis helps identify peak shopping periods and supports decisions related to staffing, inventory availability, and checkout capacity.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T16:54:28+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h3>4.1 Hourly Transaction Activity</h3>\n<h4>Business Question</h4>\n<p>During which hours of the day does the retailer experience the highest transaction activity and revenue?</p>\n<h4>Analysis Method</h4>\n<p>The transaction timestamp is used to extract the hour of each transaction.</p>\n<p>For each hour, the analysis calculates:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Number of transactions</li>\n<li>Total quantity purchased</li>\n<li>Total revenue</li>\n<li>Average transaction value</li>\n</ul>\n<p>This analysis helps identify peak shopping periods and supports decisions related to staffing, inventory availability, and checkout capacity.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785084860366_583697125","id":"paragraph_1785084860366_583697125","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T16:54:20+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T16:54:28+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T16:54:29+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%jdbc(hive)\n\nSELECT\n    transaction_id,\n    transaction_timestamp,\n    HOUR(transaction_timestamp) AS transaction_hour\nFROM transaction_summary\nLIMIT 10;","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T16:54:40+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"sql","editOnDblCli