file_path = \"/tmp/transaction_summary.csv\"\n\ndf = pd.read_csv(file_path)\n\nprint(\"Rows loaded:\", len(df))\nprint(\"Columns:\", list(df.columns))\n\ndf.head()","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T18:30:18+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"python","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"Rows loaded: 12725\nColumns: ['transaction_id', 'store_id', 'store_region', 'loyalty_flag', 'payment_type', 'total_quantity', 'distinct_products', 'transaction_value']\n  transaction_id    store_id  ... distinct_products transaction_value\n0    TXN-0000001  ST-TOR-001  ...                 2             47.22\n1    TXN-0000002  ST-TOR-001  ...                 1              6.35\n2    TXN-0000003  ST-TOR-001  ...                 2             70.91\n3    TXN-0000004  ST-TOR-001  ...                 2             20.64\n4    TXN-0000005  ST-TOR-001  ...                 3             59.80\n\n[5 rows x 8 columns]\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785090589288_1608798022","id":"paragraph_1785090589288_1608798022","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T18:29:49+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T18:30:18+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T18:30:18+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%python\n\nnumeric_columns = [\n    \"transaction_value\",\n    \"total_quantity\",\n    \"distinct_products\"\n]\n\nfor column in numeric_columns:\n    df[column] = pd.to_numeric(df[column], errors=\"coerce\")\n\nprint(df.dtypes)\nprint()\nprint(\"Missing numeric values:\")\nprint(df[numeric_columns].isnull().sum())","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T18:28:14+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"python","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"transaction_id        object\nstore_id              object\nstore_region          object\nloyalty_flag          object\npayment_type          object\ntotal_quantity         int64\ndistinct_products      int64\ntransaction_value    float64\ndtype: object\n\nMissing numeric values:\ntransaction_value    0\ntotal_quantity       0\ndistinct_products    0\ndtype: int64\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785090155212_906196921","id":"paragraph_1785090155212_906196921","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T18:22:35+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T18:28:14+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T18:28:14+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n## Python Data Validation\n\nThe Python DataFrame contains **12,725 transaction-level records**.\n\nThe fields `total_quantity` and `distinct_products` were validated as integer values, while `transaction_value` was validated as a floating-point numeric value.\n\nNo missing values were found in the three numeric analysis fields. Therefore, the transaction-level data is ready for descriptive statistics, distribution analysis, and outlier detection.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T18:29:36+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>Python Data Validation</h2>\n<p>The Python DataFrame contains <strong>12,725 transaction-level records</strong>.</p>\n<p>The fields <code>total_quantity</code> and <code>distinct_products</code> were validated as integer values, while <code>transaction_value</code> was validated as a floating-point numeric value.</p>\n<p>No missing values were found in the three numeric analysis fields. Therefore, the transaction-level data is ready for descriptive statistics, distribution analysis, and outlier detection.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785090173738_1199320850","id":"paragraph_1785090173738_1199320850","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T18:22:53+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T18:29:36+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T18:29:36+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%python\n\ntransaction_stats = df[\n    [\n        \"transaction_value\",\n        \"total_quantity\",\n        \"distinct_products\"\n    ]\n].describe().round(2)\n\ntransaction_stats","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T18:34:52+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"python","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"       transaction_value  total_quantity  distinct_products\ncount           12725.00        12725.00           12725.00\nmean               42.42            4.63               3.00\nstd                27.08            2.55               1.39\nmin                 1.85            1.00               1.00\n25%                21.87            3.00               2.00\n50%                37.55            4.00               3.00\n75%                57.85            6.00               4.00\nmax               201.09           18.00               7.00\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785090576013_1000430039","id":"paragraph_1785090576013_1000430039","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T18:29:36+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T18:34:52+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T18:34:52+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%python\n\ntransaction_values = df[\"transaction_value\"].dropna()\n\nsummary = {\n    \"count\": int(transaction_values.count()),\n    \"mean\": round(transaction_values.mean(), 2),\n    \"median\": round(transaction_values.median(), 2),\n    \"standard_deviation\": round(transaction_values.std(), 2),\n    \"minimum\": round(transaction_values.min(), 2),\n    \"maximum\": round(transaction_values.max(), 2),\n    \"q1\": round(transaction_values.quantile(0.25), 2),\n    \"q3\": round(transaction_values.quantile(0.75), 2),\n    \"iqr\": round(\n        transaction_values.quantile(0.75)\n        - transaction_values.quantile(0.25),\n        2\n    )\n}\n\nsummary","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T18:35:06+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"python","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"{'count': 12725, 'mean': np.float64(42.42), 'median': np.float64(37.55), 'standard_deviation': np.float64(27.08), 'minimum': np.float64(1.85), 'maximum': np.float64(201.09), 'q1': np.float64(21.87), 'q3': np.float64(57.85), 'iqr': np.float64(35.98)}\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785090892953_1830420542","id":"paragraph_1785090892953_1830420542","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T18:34:52+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T18:35:06+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T18:35:06+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n## Descriptive Statistics Interpretation\n\nThe transaction dataset contains **12,725 transactions**.\n\nThe average transaction value was approximately **$42.42**, while the median transaction value was approximately **$37.55**.\n\nThe standard deviation was approximately **$27.08**, indicating the amount of variation in customer spending.\n\nTransaction values ranged from approximately **$1.85** to **$201.09**.\n\nThe first quartile was approximately **$21.87**, while the third quartile was approximately **$57.85**. Therefore, the middle 50% of transaction values fell within this range.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T18:38:05+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>Descriptive Statistics Interpretation</h2>\n<p>The transaction dataset contains <strong>12,725 transactions</strong>.</p>\n<p>The average transaction value was approximately <strong>$42.42</strong>, while the median transaction value was approximately <strong>$37.55</strong>.</p>\n<p>The standard deviation was approximately <strong>$27.08</strong>, indicating the amount of variation in customer spending.</p>\n<p>Transaction values ranged from approximately <strong>$1.85</strong> to <strong>$201.09</strong>.</p>\n<p>The first quartile was approximately <strong>$21.87</strong>, while the third quartile was approximately <strong>$57.85</strong>. Therefore, the middle 50% of transaction values fell within this range.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785090906474_698910118","id":"paragraph_1785090906474_698910118","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T18:35:06+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T18:38:05+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T18:38:05+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%python\n\nimport pandas as pd\n\ntransaction_values = df[\"transaction_value\"].dropna()\n\nhistogram = pd.cut(\n    transaction_values,\n    bins=15\n).value_counts().sort_index()\n\nhistogram_df = histogram.reset_index()\nhistogram_df.columns = [\n    \"transaction_value_range\",\n    \"frequency\"\n]\n\nhistogram_df[\"transaction_value_range\"] = (\n    histogram_df[\"transaction_value_range\"]\n    .astype(str)\n)\n\nhistogram_df","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T18:40:25+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"python","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"   transaction_value_range  frequency\n0          (1.651, 15.133]       1884\n1         (15.133, 28.415]       2612\n2         (28.415, 41.698]       2606\n3         (41.698, 54.981]       2093\n4         (54.981, 68.263]       1445\n5         (68.263, 81.546]        906\n6         (81.546, 94.829]        599\n7        (94.829, 108.111]        309\n8       (108.111, 121.394]        134\n9       (121.394, 134.677]         74\n10      (134.677, 147.959]         26\n11      (147.959, 161.242]         13\n12      (161.242, 174.525]         18\n13      (174.525, 187.807]          4\n14       (187.807, 201.09]          2\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785091085060_259229680","id":"paragraph_1785091085060_259229680","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T18:38:05+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T18:40:25+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T18:40:25+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n## Transaction Value Distribution\n\nThe transaction-value distribution is concentrated mainly in the lower and middle value ranges.\n\nThe number of transactions decreases as transaction value increases, creating a longer tail toward the higher-value ranges.\n\nThis pattern indicates a right-skewed distribution. Most customers complete moderate-value transactions, while a smaller number of customers make unusually large purchases.\n\nBecause these high-value transactions can increase the mean, both the mean and median should be considered when describing typical customer spending.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T18:41:03+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>Transaction Value Distribution</h2>\n<p>The transaction-value distribution is concentrated mainly in the lower and middle value ranges.</p>\n<p>The number of transactions decreases as transaction value increases, creating a longer tail toward the higher-value ranges.</p>\n<p>This pattern indicates a right-skewed distribution. Most customers complete moderate-value transactions, while a smaller number of customers make unusually large purchases.</p>\n<p>Because these high-value transactions can increase the mean, both the mean and median should be considered when describing typical customer spending.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785091162264_1680139310","id":"paragraph_1785091162264_1680139310","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T18:39:22+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T18:41:03+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T18:41:03+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%python\n\ntransaction_values = df[\"transaction_value\"].dropna()\n\nq1 = transaction_values.quantile(0.25)\nq3 = transaction_values.quantile(0.75)\niqr = q3 - q1\n\nlower_bound = q1 - 1.5 * iqr\nupper_bound = q3 + 1.5 * iqr\n\noutliers = df[\n    (df[\"transaction_value\"] < lower_bound)\n    | (df[\"transaction_value\"] > upper_bound)\n].copy()\n\noutlier_percentage = len(outliers) / len(df) * 100\n\nprint(\"Q1:\", round(q1, 2))\nprint(\"Q3:\", round(q3, 2))\nprint(\"IQR:\", round(iqr, 2))\nprint(\"Lower bound:\", round(lower_bound, 2))\nprint(\"Upper bound:\", round(upper_bound, 2))\nprint(\"Number of outliers:\", len(outliers))\nprint(\"Outlier percentage:\", round(outlier_percentage, 2), \"%\")","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T18:51:42+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"python","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"Q1: 21.87\nQ3: 57.85\nIQR: 35.98\nLower bound: -32.1\nUpper bound: 111.82\nNumber of outliers: 216\nOutlier percentage: 1.7 \n%\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785091263096_2145644583","id":"paragraph_1785091263096_2145644583","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T18:41:03+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T18:51:42+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T18:51:42+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n## IQR Outlier Analysis\n\nThe interquartile range method was used to identify unusually high or low transaction values.\n\nThe first quartile was **$21.87**, and the third quartile was **$57.85**, resulting in an interquartile range of **35.98**.\n\nTransactions below **$-32.1** or above **$111.82** were classified as potential outliers.\n\nA total of **216** transactions were identified as potential outliers, representing approximately **1.7%** of all transactions.\n\nThese records should not automatically be treated as data errors. High-value outliers may represent legitimate large purchases, while unusually low transaction values may reflect small purchases, discounts, returns, or other special transaction conditions.\n\nFurther investigation would be required before removing or correcting any outlier records.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T19:18:05+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>IQR Outlier Analysis</h2>\n<p>The interquartile range method was used to identify unusually high or low transaction values.</p>\n<p>The first quartile was <strong>$21.87</strong>, and the third quartile was <strong>$57.85</strong>, resulting in an interquartile range of <strong>35.98</strong>.</p>\n<p>Transactions below <strong>$-32.1</strong> or above <strong>$111.82</strong> were classified as potential outliers.</p>\n<p>A total of <strong>216</strong> transactions were identified as potential outliers, representing approximately <strong>1.7%</strong> of all transactions.</p>\n<p>These records should not automatically be treated as data errors. High-value outliers may represent legitimate large purchases, while unusually low transaction values may reflect small purchases, discounts, returns, or other special transaction conditions.</p>\n<p>Further investigation would be required before removing or correcting any outlier records.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785092000304_415356926","id":"paragraph_1785092000304_415356926","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T18:53:20+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T19:18:05+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T19:18:05+0000","status":"FINISHED","focus":false},{"text":"%python\n\ntop_outliers = outliers[\n    [\n        \"transaction_id\",\n        \"store_id\",\n        \"store_region\",\n        \"total_quantity\",\n        \"distinct_products\",\n        \"transaction_value\"\n    ]\n].sort_values(\n    by=\"transaction_value\",\n    ascending=False\n).head(10)\n\ntop_outliers","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T18:51:52+0000","progress":0,"config":{"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"results":{},"enabled":true,"editorSetting":{"language":"python","editOnDblClick":false,"completionSupport":true}},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"TEXT","data":"      transaction_id    store_id  ... distinct_products  transaction_value\n11540    TXN-0011541  ST-CAL-001  ...                 7             201.09\n2110     TXN-0002111  ST-CAL-001  ...                 6             198.15\n11934    TXN-0011935  ST-KIT-001  ...                 7             186.00\n6508     TXN-0006509  ST-SCA-001  ...                 7             183.16\n9966     TXN-0009967  ST-OTT-001  ...                 7             180.63\n7038     TXN-0007039  ST-KIT-001  ...                 7             179.64\n8924     TXN-0008925  ST-OTT-001  ...                 7             173.72\n8735     TXN-0008736  ST-KIT-001  ...                 7             172.97\n1949     TXN-0001950  ST-CAL-001  ...                 6             172.62\n1515     TXN-0001516  ST-EDM-001  ...                 7             169.82\n\n[10 rows x 6 columns]\n"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785091902183_1399063528","id":"paragraph_1785091902183_1399063528","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T18:51:42+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T18:51:52+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T18:51:52+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n# Master Task 10 — Python Statistical Analytics Summary\n\n## Completed Analysis\n\nThe Python statistical analysis included:\n\n1. Loading **12,725 transaction-level records**\n2. Validating numeric data types\n3. Confirming that no missing values were present in the main numeric fields\n4. Calculating descriptive statistics for transaction value, total quantity, and distinct products\n5. Comparing the mean, median, standard deviation, minimum, maximum, and quartiles\n6. Creating a transaction-value frequency distribution table\n7. Identifying potential outliers using the interquartile range method\n8. Reviewing the highest-value transaction outliers\n\n## Key Findings\n\nThe statistical analysis showed the typical spending level and the amount of variation across customer transactions.\n\nThe frequency distribution indicated that most transactions were concentrated in the lower and middle value ranges, while fewer transactions appeared in the highest-value ranges.\n\nThe IQR method identified transactions outside the normal transaction-value range. These records were retained because unusually high or low values may represent legitimate customer behavior rather than data-quality errors.\n\n## Business Implications\n\nThe mean and median should both be considered when describing typical customer spending because high-value transactions can influence the average.\n\nHigh-value outliers may represent important customer segments or large basket purchases. These transactions could be investigated further to understand the products, stores, regions, and customer characteristics associated with unusually large purchases.\n\nThe Python results complement the HiveQL analysis by explaining the distribution and variability of transaction values rather than focusing only on total revenue and rankings.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T18:57:12+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h1>Master Task 10 — Python Statistical Analytics Summary</h1>\n<h2>Completed Analysis</h2>\n<p>The Python statistical analysis included:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Loading <strong>12,725 transaction-level records</strong></li>\n<li>Validating numeric data types</li>\n<li>Confirming that no missing values were present in the main numeric fields</li>\n<li>Calculating descriptive statistics for transaction value, total quantity, and distinct products</li>\n<li>Comparing the mean, median, standard deviation, minimum, maximum, and quartiles</li>\n<li>Creating a transaction-value frequency distribution table</li>\n<li>Identifying potential outliers using the interquartile range method</li>\n<li>Reviewing the highest-value transaction outliers</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Key Findings</h2>\n<p>The statistical analysis showed the typical spending level and the amount of variation across customer transactions.</p>\n<p>The frequency distribution indicated that most transactions were concentrated in the lower and middle value ranges, while fewer transactions appeared in the highest-value ranges.</p>\n<p>The IQR method identified transactions outside the normal transaction-value range. These records were retained because unusually high or low values may represent legitimate customer behavior rather than data-quality errors.</p>\n<h2>Business Implications</h2>\n<p>The mean and median should both be considered when describing typical customer spending because high-value transactions can influence the average.</p>\n<p>High-value outliers may represent important customer segments or large basket purchases. These transactions could be investigated further to understand the products, stores, regions, and customer characteristics associated with unusually large purchases.</p>\n<p>The Python results complement the HiveQL analysis by explaining the distribution and variability of transaction values rather than focusing only on total revenue and rankings.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785091989834_1851621661","id":"paragraph_1785091989834_1851621661","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T18:53:09+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T18:57:12+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T18:57:12+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n# Master Task 11 — Integrated Investigation\n\nHiveQL was used to analyze store, regional, time, category, and promotion performance.\n\nPython was used to analyze transaction-value distribution and identify potential outliers.\n\nThe combined analysis provides both business-level findings and transaction-level statistical evidence.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T19:01:17+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h1>Master Task 11 — Integrated Investigation</h1>\n<p>HiveQL was used to analyze store, regional, time, category, and promotion performance.</p>\n<p>Python was used to analyze transaction-value distribution and identify potential outliers.</p>\n<p>The combined analysis provides both business-level findings and transaction-level statistical evidence.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785092232522_928147775","id":"paragraph_1785092232522_928147775","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T18:57:12+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T19:01:17+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T19:01:17+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n## Key Findings\n\n- **ST-CAL-001** generated the highest store revenue: **$55,573.77**\n- **ST-CAL-001** completed **1,167 transactions**\n- Its average transaction value was **$47.62**\n- Its revenue was **23.56% above** the average store revenue\n\n- **ST-KIT-001** had the largest negative deviation: **-$7,102.69**, or **-15.79%**\n\n- Average revenue per store was **$44,977.58**\n\n- The **Central region** generated the highest total revenue\n- The **Western region** had the highest average revenue per store: **$50,941.11**\n\n- Peak transaction hour: **18:00**\n- Transactions at 18:00: **1,809**\n- Revenue at 18:00: **$76,526.71**\n\n- **Sunday** had the highest transaction count: **2,106**\n- **Saturday** had the highest daily revenue: **$90,570.71**\n\n- **Grocery generated** the highest promotional revenue: **$3,962.47**\n- Promotional revenue represented only **2.31%** of Grocery revenue\n\n- Python identified **216 potential outliers**\n- Outliers represented **1.70%** of all transactions\n- The upper outlier threshold was **$111.82**\n- The transaction-value distribution was right-skewed","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T19:03:19+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>Key Findings</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>ST-CAL-001</strong> generated the highest store revenue: <strong>$55,573.77</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>ST-CAL-001</strong> completed <strong>1,167 transactions</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Its average transaction value was <strong>$47.62</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Its revenue was <strong>23.56% above</strong> the average store revenue</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>ST-KIT-001</strong> had the largest negative deviation: <strong>-$7,102.69</strong>, or <strong>-15.79%</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Average revenue per store was <strong>$44,977.58</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The <strong>Central region</strong> generated the highest total revenue</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The <strong>Western region</strong> had the highest average revenue per store: <strong>$50,941.11</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Peak transaction hour: <strong>18:00</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Transactions at 18:00: <strong>1,809</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Revenue at 18:00: <strong>$76,526.71</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Sunday</strong> had the highest transaction count: <strong>2,106</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Saturday</strong> had the highest daily revenue: <strong>$90,570.71</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Grocery generated</strong> the highest promotional revenue: <strong>$3,962.47</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Promotional revenue represented only <strong>2.31%</strong> of Grocery revenue</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Python identified <strong>216 potential outliers</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Outliers represented <strong>1.70%</strong> of all transactions</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The upper outlier threshold was <strong>$111.82</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>The transaction-value distribution was right-skewed</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785092294109_1180061980","id":"paragraph_1785092294109_1180061980","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T18:58:14+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T19:03:19+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T19:03:19+0000","status":"FINISHED"},{"text":"%md\n\n## Recommendations\n\n1. Study the product mix, customer traffic, and operations of **ST-CAL-001** and apply successful practices to weaker stores.\n\n2. Review **ST-KIT-001** to identify possible issues involving traffic, inventory, product mix, or local demand.\n\n3. Increase staffing, inventory availability, and checkout capacity during weekends and around **18:00**.\n\n4. Evaluate promotions using revenue, profit margin, transaction count, and customer response instead of promotional revenue alone.\n\n5. Investigate the **216 high-value outliers** by store, region, category, loyalty status, and payment method.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe results show clear differences across stores, regions, time periods, and transaction values.\n\nHiveQL identified the strongest business-performance patterns, while Python showed that most transactions were in the lower and middle ranges, with a small number of high-value purchases.\n\nManagement should focus on high-performing store practices, weak-store improvement, weekend and evening operations, and high-value customer behavior.","user":"anonymous","dateUpdated":"2026-07-26T19:04:24+0000","progress":0,"config":{"tableHide":false,"editorSetting":{"language":"markdown","editOnDblClick":true,"completionSupport":false},"colWidth":12,"fontSize":9,"editorHide":true,"results":{},"enabled":true},"settings":{"params":{},"forms":{}},"results":{"code":"SUCCESS","msg":[{"type":"HTML","data":"<div class=\"markdown-body\">\n<h2>Recommendations</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p>Study the product mix, customer traffic, and operations of <strong>ST-CAL-001</strong> and apply successful practices to weaker stores.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Review <strong>ST-KIT-001</strong> to identify possible issues involving traffic, inventory, product mix, or local demand.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Increase staffing, inventory availability, and checkout capacity during weekends and around <strong>18:00</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Evaluate promotions using revenue, profit margin, transaction count, and customer response instead of promotional revenue alone.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Investigate the <strong>216 high-value outliers</strong> by store, region, category, loyalty status, and payment method.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Conclusion</h2>\n<p>The results show clear differences across stores, regions, time periods, and transaction values.</p>\n<p>HiveQL identified the strongest business-performance patterns, while Python showed that most transactions were in the lower and middle ranges, with a small number of high-value purchases.</p>\n<p>Management should focus on high-performing store practices, weak-store improvement, weekend and evening operations, and high-value customer behavior.</p>\n\n</div>"}]},"apps":[],"runtimeInfos":{},"progressUpdateIntervalMs":500,"jobName":"paragraph_1785092339313_810988900","id":"paragraph_1785092339313_810988900","dateCreated":"2026-07-26T18:58:59+0000","dateStarted":"2026-07-26T19:04:24+0000","dateFinished":"2026-07-26T19:04:24+0000","status":"FINISHED"}],"name":"Loblaw_HBase_Hive_Analytics","id":"2MXY3PHYZ","defaultInterpreterGroup":"python","version":"0.12.0","noteParams":{},"noteForms":{},"angularObjects":{},"config":{"isZeppelinNotebookCronEnable":false,"looknfeel":"default","personalizedMode":"false"},"info":{},"path":"/Loblaw_HBase_Hive_Analytics"}